ABUNDANT ABUNDANT-STEP ABUNDANTSTEP

   This skill will allow you to designate a list of directions for your
character to follow, which if valid will result in your character skipping the
rooms (and even doors!  ) in between.  You will then reappear at your designated
location

Usage: abundantstep <direction string>
IE: abundantstep 2w n e d
#0
AC AC-APPLY ARMOR-APPLY ARMOR-CLASS ARMOR-RATING ARMORCLASS ARMORINFO ARMORING


Your Armor Class (often called AC) is an expression for how good your armor
is at protecting you.  When you don armor, any AC apply that armor has is 
added to your standard (naked) AC value.

**NOTE**  Internally values are stored as a factor of 10 since our
equipment system has a lot more slots than a normal DnD type system
would have.  When you type score though, the value you see for your
AC will include all converions.

You can use the 'armorlist' command to see all the armor types
You can use the 'armorinfo <armor type name>' command to get details about armor types

	YARMOR	n
Class  AC  Armor        Max Dex  Check Pnlty  Cast Pnlty  Weight
----------------------------------------------------------------
None   0   None         No Cap   None         None        0  lbs
Light  1   Padded       8        None         5%          10 lbs
Light  2   Leather      6        None         10%         15 lbs
Light  3   Studded      4        -1           20%         25 lbs
Medium 4   Chain        4        -2           20%         25 lbs
Medium 5   Breastplate  2        -5           30%         40 lbs
Heavy  6   Splint       1        -7           40%         45 lbs
Heavy  7   Halfplate    0        -7           40%         50 lbs
Heavy  8   Fullplate    1        -8           45%         50 lbs

	YSHIELDS	n
