#0
AOE AOE-SPELLS

AOE stands for 'area of effect.'  Which means that the effect(s) of the
spell will affect everyone in the room.  If the spell is hostile, it
will not affect members of your group or CHARMEE followers of your
group members.

See also:  CHARMEE
#0
AOE-BOMBS AOEBOMBS

Bombs are a staple tool of the adventuring alchemist.  However, sometimes alchemists
may want to contain the effects of their bomb to a single target, and other times
they seek to have a wider area of affect.

Typing AOEBOMBS will toggle this affect on and off.

In the prefedit command menu, there is an option for AOEBOMBS.  This is disabled
by default.  When disabled, your bombs will only affect a single target, and will not
have any secondary effects.  When enabled, the bombs will hit all non-party-members
in the room, mobs and pcs both.  The full effect of the bomb will only occur on
the primary target, while secondary effects will occur on all other eligible targets
in the room.
#0
APOTHEOSIS ARCANE-APOTHEOSIS

This ability, unique to sorcerers with the arcane bloodline, allows powering wands and staves with spell slots.

When you use this command, you will gain a number of Apotheosis points equal to the level of the circle you sacrifice to it.  If you have at least three points saved up, then your next activation of a wand or staff will consume three points instead of one charge from the magical item.  Points are not lost over time, but will be removed if you start to 'meditate' to regain your spells.  
You can check how many points you have stored up by using the 'meditate' command while not resting.  


Usage: apotheosis <circle>

See also: feat info arcane apotheosis
