#0
ARCANA-SKILL SKILL-ARCANA ARCANA

\n   Your arcana skill measures your ability to recall lore about spells, magic\nitems, eldritch symbols, magical traditions, the planes of existence, and the\ninhabitants of those planes.\n\nIt can also be used to identify items and creatures. (HELP LORE)\n\n

#0
ARCANA-BLOODLINE ARCANE-BLOODLINE BLOODLINE-ARCANA BLOODLINE-ARCANE SORCERER-BLOODLINE-ARCANA SORCERER-BLOODLINE-ARCANE


Sorcerers have the option to select a bloodline that explains where their
magical prowess comes from.  The arcane bloodline is developed through a long
heritage of masterful arcane spellcasters whose gift has passed on to manifest
naturally within the sorcerer. The arcane bloodline offers additional spell
knowledge, increased metamagic prowess, enhanced ability in a school of choice
and an innate ability to use consumable magic such as wands and staves. 
 
The arcane bloodline is associated with a specific school of spellcasting. Some
of the arcane bloodline abilities will offer benefits specific to this school.
 
NEW CLASS SKILL: Appraise
BONUS SPELLS: identify (3rd), invisibility (5th), dispel magic (7th), minor 
globe (9th), feeblemind (11th), true seeing (13th), teleport (15th), power 
word stun (17th), time stop (19th).
 
CLASS FEATS: combat casting, improved counterspell, improved initiative, iron will,
scribe scroll, skill focus, spell focus, still spell.
 
The arcane bloodline also gives the following bonus abilities:
Improved familiar feat at sorcerer level 1. (HELP IMPROVED FAMILIAR)
Metamagic adept feat at sorcerer level 3. (HELP METAMAGIC ADEPT)
New arcana feats at sorcerer levels 9, 13, and 17. (HELP NEW ARCANA)
School power at sorcerer level 15. (HELP SCHOOL POWER)
Arcane apotheosis feat at sorcerer level 20. (HELP ARCANE APOTHEOSIS)
 
See Also: SORCERER

#0
ARCANE-CASTING

Arcane casting is defined as magic cast by Wizard, Sorcerer, Bard
and other related classes.  The two major classes of magic is
Arcane (Or 'Magical') and Divine.  Arcane spells tend to be more
offensive in nature while Divine spells tend to be more beneficial
in nature.

See Also:  DIVINE-CASTING
#0
ARCANE-SPELL-FAILURE SPELL-FAILURE


   Most arcane spellcasting classes require unobstructed movement in order to
successfully cast their spells.  As such, when they wear armor, this limits
their ability to cast arcane spells.  The heavier the armor, the greater the
chance that they will fail when casting an arcane spell.  Warlocks, bards and
summoners have the ability to wear light armor without suffering any failure
chance.  There are also other feats and class abilities that will reduce the
chance of arcane spell failure.

#0
AOE AREA-AFFECT

AOE stands for "Area of Effect"

Area-affect spells are spells that will target everything in the room.

A harmful area-affect spell will target everyone not-grouped, regardless
if they are friendly or not.  A positive area-affect spell will target
everyone in your group whom is in the immediate area.

Be very careful when firing off harmful area-affect spells, you could
possibly start a fight with someone you don't want to.

See Also:  SPELLS
#0
AREA-BETHEL-ISLAND BETHEL-ISLAND

   Bethel Island is a small fishing and farming island north of Palanthas in the\nBay of Branchala.  It can be reached via any sailing dock using the 'sail'\ncommand.\n

#0
AREA-CULTISTS-OF-MORGION CULTISTS-OF-MORGION

   Rumour has it that there is a hidden cultist encampment devoted to followers\nof the evil god, Morgion, somewhere in Solamnia between Vingaard Keep and\nPalanthas.  That Morgion, the god of disease and suffering, has a foothold in\nSolamnia is of great concern to the Solamnic Knights and the Forces of\nWhitestone.\n

#0
AREA-FIRESIDE-TAVERN FIRESIDE-TAVERN

   Fireside Tavern is a popular resting point for merchants and travelers\ncrossing northern Abanasinia.  It is located along the New Sea Road east and\nthen north of Solace.\n

#0
AREA-LOST-CAVERNS-OF-PALANTHAS LOST-CAVERNS-OF-PALANTHAS

   Palanthas is an ancient city and with it come ancient myths and legends.  \nOnce such legend is that of a complex of hidden caves and caverns where\ncreatures of evil and malice reside, trapped in long ago by the Master of the\nTower of High Sorcery in Palanthas, centuries before the reign of Istar and the\ncataclysm.  It's entrance is unknown, though it's rumoured that some buildings\nwithin the city may stand on top of ancient entrances.\n

#0
AREA-PALANTHAS PALANTHAS

   Palanthas, also called Palanthas the Ancient and Palanthas the Beautiful, is\none of the largest cities in Ansalon.  It lies nestled safely in the Bay of\nBranchala in the northwest corner of the Ansalon mainland, protected from the\nfurious Turbidus Ocean.  It is home to more than 32,000 citizens most of whom\nare humans, the rest a mix of other races such as elves, dwarves, gnomes, and\nthe occasional minotaur and kender.  The Cityhome has long been the pride of\nSolamnia, hailed as one of the major beacons of light in the world and with its\nwhite marble buildings and magnificent villas it is a beautiful sight indeed.  \nThe city relies heavily on trade with merchants from all over Ansalon.  Even\nminotaur vessels are allowed through the Gates of Paladine.\n\nPalanthas is generally considered a city of morally good citizens,\nand is the home of the Knights of Solamnia and Forces of Whitestone.\n\nSee Also:\nAREA-BETHEL-ISLAND\nAREA-DRACONIAN-SMUGGLERS-BASE\nAREA-GARDENS-OF-THE-BLUE-PHOENIX\nAREA-PALANTHAS-GRAVEYARD\nAREA-PALANTHAS-SEWERS\nAREA-PALANTHAS-SHOPS\nAREA-PALANTHAS-THIEVES-GUILD\nAREA-PALANTHAS-TRAINING-PIT\nAREA-THE-PALACE-OF-PALANTHAS\nAREA-THE-PALANTHAS-WIZARD-ACADEMY\n\n

