#0
ARTIFACT ARTIFACTS

Usage: artifact
       artifact list
       artifact info <item>
       artifact progress
       artifact abilities

   Artifacts are unique items of power. Each one exists only once in the
world - if someone else holds it, it will not appear again until they let it
go. Artifacts grow stronger as they are used, rising from level 1 to level 5,
and every bonus they grant scales with that level.

   Many artifacts bind themselves to a single owner. A bind-on-pickup
artifact claims you the moment you take it; a bind-on-equip artifact waits
until you first wear it; a bind-on-account artifact can be shared between
your own characters. A bound artifact will not answer to anyone else.

   Some artifacts grant an ability you invoke by name, such as SOULSTRIKE,
DIVINEWARD, or DOOMBLAST. Use 'artifact abilities' to see which of yours are
ready.

   Some artifacts grant always-on senses, speed, or protections simply for
being worn. 'artifact info <item>' shows every active and locked power. If
that section is absent, the artifact grants no hidden always-on states.

   A few artifacts are sworn to a single class and demand real depth in it.
Wear one without that depth and it will burn you every tick you keep it on.
It will not reveal or answer its called words or its active command.

   Artifact weapons may also carry signature strikes that trigger during
combat. Most use the same internal recharge as their other weapon procs, but
true per-hit effects roll independently, and some protect against long streaks
of failed rolls. Use 'artifact info <item>' to see the chance and exact
behavior of a signature strike once you hold the artifact.

   The generic percentage shown under Combat is a per-hit attempt rate. If
the selected effect cannot change anything, such as healing a bearer already
at full health, the artifact spends no internal recharge and may try again on
a later hit.

   Avernus carries both kinds of power. Its Bladesong may heal or pull its
wielder out of an ordinary knockdown on any successful hit. Separately, it
rolls 1-in-31 to steal life from a living foe for triple damage. This named
strike does not consume or wait on Avernus's generic artifact-proc timer.

   Earthcrier has an 8 percent chance per successful damaging hit to force a
Reflex save against DC 21 plus its artifact level plus the wielder's current
Strength and Constitution bonuses. Its signature requires a non-good wielder
and has a 30-second internal recharge. Earthcrier has no generic artifact proc.
No-bash, free-moving, incorporeal, and already-down foes are immune. Use
'artifact info earthcrier' to see your current DC.

> artifact list
> artifact info doombringer
> artifact progress

See also: SOULSTRIKE, DIVINEWARD, DOOMBLAST
#0
ASSIST

Usage: assist <player>

   If <player> needs assistance in battle and you feel brave enough to help, 
use this command to join the battle. The monster attacking <player> will keep 
hitting them, unless it decides to switch.

> assist tink

See also: AUTO, FLEE, KILL, RESCUE
#0
DOOMBLAST DIVINEWARD SOULSTRIKE

Usage: soulstrike [target]
       divineward
       doomblast

   These are artifact abilities. Each one only works while you have the
artifact that grants it equipped, and each costs psionic energy and has its
own cooldown.

   A class-sworn artifact grants its active command only to a bearer it
recognizes. A rejected command costs no energy and starts no cooldown.

   SOULSTRIKE hurls a bolt of soul energy at a single target. DIVINEWARD
wraps you in a sanctuary of divine light. DOOMBLAST unleashes a wave of doom
on everyone hostile in the room.

   Using an artifact ability also feeds experience to the artifact itself.

See also: ARTIFACT
