#0
ATTACK-QUEUE

	n
	YAttack Queue	n
	n
Usage: attackqueue / attackqueue clear

Assuming you don't use any of your actions, your default attack in combat
will be your full melee attack rotation.  Some forms of attacks do not
consume any actions points (such as standard action), but instead will
consume one of your melee attacks.  So if in a normal 6 second round you
would normally get 3 attacks, and you use one of these special attacks, you
would get 2 attacks plus perform the special attack.  Without any consumption
of any of your action points.
	n
	YSee also:	n 	Raction queue	n, 	Rcombat	n
	n
#0
ATTACK-ROLL

Your attack roll is your base-attack-bonus (BAB) + hitroll.  Your BAB
is determined by your level and class, your hitroll is your strength
bonus, skill-bonuses, gear-bonuses.  This value is compared to an
opponents armor-class (AC) when determining whether your blow lands or
not.
See also:  BAB FINESSE SKILLS HITROLL AC
#0
ATTACK-QUEUE ATTACKQUEUE

   The attack queue allows you to enter commands that will fire during combat.
You can pre-load your queue with combat manuevers, spells, abilities, etc.

Certain commands, such as "treat wounds", fleeing or recalling will interrupt
your queue.

SEE ALSO: Combat Manuevers
