AUTOCOLLECT

The AutoCollect toggle will cause the player to perform the 'collect'
command after each kill.  This is used to gather your ammo, which helps
keep individual ammo supplies from getting mixed up.

See Also: COLLECT
#0
AUTOCONSIDER

Usage: autoconsider
       (also available in prefedit)

The autoconsider option allows you to see an indicator to the left of a mob's
name when typing 'look'.  This indicator will show either how many levels the mob
is above your own, below your own, or equal.  When a mob's level is more then 5 levels
above your own, it will display [!!].  When it is 6 levels below yours or less, it
will show [--].  If it is equal it will show [==].

#0
AUTODOOR

Usage: autodoor

When enabled this toggle will automatically find the next available door when 
using the open, close, lock, unlock or pick commands. For example, in a room 
with several closed doors, one door will be opened each time the player types 
open door until all the doors are open. The player can still specify a 
direction to open a particular door.

See Also: AUTOKEY, TOGGLE, PREFEDIT
