compromised passwords. 

#0
BACKGROUND-ARCHTYPES BACKGROUNDS

\n\nBackground archtypes represent a character's history before they became an adventurer.\nEach background offers bonuses to 2 skills and adds 1 or more special ability.\nBackgrounds can be selected from the main game menu, by selecting character options\nand then background archtypes.\n\nThe currently available backgrounds are: acolyte, charlatan, criminal, entertainer,\nfolk hero, gladiator, hermit, noble, outlander, pirate, sage, sailor, soldier, squire,\ntrader and urchin.\n\nYou can see more info on each archtype by typing HELP (background name)\n\n

#0
BACKPACK BAG

Backpack Bag
.
Your starting container is a leather backpack.  It has an alias 'bp' for convenience, i.e. you can interact with
your starting backpack with 'bp' such as 'look in backpack' or 'l in bp'
You can also RESTRING your starting container if you don't like the style.
See also: INVENTORY, RESTRING
#0
BACKSTAB

	n
Backstab, Backstab Combat Maneuver
	n
Requirements:  Piercing weapon(s), Not fighting, Opponent not fighting
Attack roll :  Normal attack roll
               +1 bonus for sneaking
               +1 bonus for hiding
               +4 bonus for backstab feat
Action      :  Full Round Action
               Has backstab feat - Move Action instead
Bonus       :  +4 damage per weapon, initiative, see below
	n
Using suprise, you are able to stab your opponent and flank them with a
special attack using piercing weapons.
	n
The advantages of using this attack over a normal attack is the ability
to stab instantly with both weapons when dual wielding, a guarantee to
automatically win initiative and a +4 bonus damage done on each attack.
	n
	YSee also: 	Rfeat info backstab	n
	n
#0
BAG-NAMES BAGNAMES BAGS SORTING


Usage: sortto (item name) bag[1-10]
        sortfrom (item name) bag[1-10]
        bags
        bag (1-10)
        bagnames (1-10) (bag nickname)
       
The sort command allows you to sort different items into different 'virtual bags'.
This is helpful in organizing your inventory.
       
Here are some examples:
sortto sword bag1          : this will put the item 'sword' into bag1.
sortfrom breastplate bag3  : this will put item 'breastplate' from bag3 into your main inventory.
sortto sword weapons       : this will put the item 'sword' into the bag nicknamed 'weapons'.
       
To view your bag contents, use:
bag 1         : this will show all items in bag 1
bag materials : this will show all items in the bag nicknamed 'materials'
       
By typing 'bags' by itself, it will show the number of items in each of your bags as
well as any nicknames associated with your bags.
       
See Also: CONTAINERS
