BLINK BLINK-AFFECTION BLINKING

	n
Blink, Blink Affection, Blinking
	n
You 'blink' quickly back and forth between the Material Plane and the Ethereal Plane and
look as though you're winking in and out of reality at random. Blink has three effects:
	n
1)  You have 20% concealment bonus against physical attacks (it does not stack with blur
or displace).
2)  You have 20% chance of dodging any Area-affect spells.
3)  Since your opponent has trouble pinning your location, you have a +2 circumstance
attack bonus against your opponent.
	n
#0
BLOOD-DRAIN DRINK-BLOOD DRINKING-BLOOD VAMPIRE-BLOOD-DRAIN VAMPIRE-FEEDING

Usage: blooddrain

A vampire has the ability to drink the blood of other creatures, in fact they
need to do so in order to survive. In order to drink another creature's
blood, the creature must first be living, and not an ooze, or shapechanged
into an ooze, construct or other creature that does not have living blood.

To initiate blood drain, the vampire needs to type the blooddrain command.
Then the blood drain will occur each round, under the following conditions:
-If the vampire is good, the target must be evil or non-sentient.
-If the vampire is not good, the target must simply be a living creature (see above).
-The vampire must be covered or not in sunlight (HELP SUNLIGHT).
-The vampire must not be in a room with moving water.

Each round of blood drain, the vampire will gain 5 hp, up to 2 x their max hp.
The target will take 5 points of blood drain damage, and if they fail a
fortitude save, they'll take 1-4 point of constitution damage. If their
constitution drops to zero, they will be paralyzed until their constitution
rises above zero (through restoration type spells mainly).

See Also: RECENTLY FED, BLOOD STARVED, VAMPIRE

#0
BLOODLINE SORCERER-BLOODLINE

   Filled with magical power that screams for release, sorcery is not so much a
calling as a blessingor a curse.  For some sorcerers, this arcane birthright
manifests in subtle and carefully controlled ways, assisting in their
manipulation of others or the pursuit of lofty goals.  For others, it is wild
and unpredictable, the primal and explosive lashing out of a power greater than
themselves.  Presented below are a number of bloodlines representing the
mysterious origin of your sorcerers abilities.

You will see a list of bloodline options for sorcerer in the STUDY menu.

See also:  <name of bloodline>-BLOODLINE

