#0
BOARD BOARDHOSTILE BOARD_HOSTILE CONTACTS DISEMBARK DOCK HEADING LOOKOUTSIDE LOOK_OUTSIDE SETSAIL SHIPSTATUS SHIPROOMS SHIP_ROOMS SPEED TACTICAL UNDOCK VESSEL VESSELS

Vessel navigation and boarding:

BOARD [vessel]
  Board a vessel object in your room.

DISEMBARK
  Leave a stopped vessel. Docked ships return you safely to the dock or linked
  ship. Away from shore, you must be able to swim and will enter the water.

TACTICAL / SHIPSTATUS / CONTACTS
  Show the local terrain grid, vessel condition, or nearby vessels.

SPEED [0-max] / HEADING [0-360]
  Set speed or an absolute compass heading at an authorized helm.

SETSAIL <direction>
  Set a cardinal, diagonal, up, or down heading and begin moving. The vessel
  must already have a positive speed.

DOCK [vessel] / UNDOCK
  List nearby targets or create/remove a gangway between stopped vessels.

LOOK_OUTSIDE / SHIP_ROOMS
  Inspect the exterior or list the vessel interior, bridge, and entrance.

BOARD_HOSTILE <vessel>
  Attempt a hostile transfer from one nearby vessel to another. Player-owned
  targets remain subject to the shared PvP consent rules.

Navigation changes require the owner, a permitted helmsman, or the authorized
NPC pilot at the helm.

See also: AUTOPILOT, SHIP-COMBAT, SHIP-OWNERSHIP, SEASTATE, VEHICLES

