#0
BONUS BONUS-TYPES

Bonuses are numerical values that are added to checks and statistical scores. 
Most bonuses have a type, and as a general rule, bonuses of the same type are 
not cumulative (do not stack)  only the greater bonus granted applies.
 
The important aspect of bonus types is that two bonuses of the same type don't 
generally stack. With the exception of dodge bonuses, circumstance bonuses, and
racial bonuses, only the better bonus of a given type works.   Bonuses without 
a type always stack.
 
Luminari uses the following bonus types:

- Alchemical (modifies Ability Scores)
- Armor (modifies AC)
- Circumstance (modifies Attacks and Checks)
- Competence (modifies Attacks, Checks and Saves)
- Deflection (modifies AC)
- Dodge (modifies AC)
- Enhancement (modifies Ability Scores, AC, Attacks, Damage and Speed)
- Inherent (modifies Ability Scores)
- Insight (modifies AC, Attacks, Checks and Saves)
- Luck (modifies AC, Attacks, Checks, Damage and Saves)
- Morale (modifies Attacks, Checks, Damage, Saves, Str, Con and Dex)
- Natural Armor (modifies AC)
- Profane (modifies AC, Checks, Damage, DCs and Saves)
- Racial (modifies Any)
- Resistance (modifies Saves)
- Sacred (modifies AC, Checks, Damage, DCs and Saves)
- Shield (modifies AC)
- Size (modifies Ability Scores, Attacks and AC)

