#0
BONUS-STAT-CAP-SYSTEM

	n
There are two values relevant to a character for each stat.  First
is the 'real' value, which is basically a characters natural stats.
Second there is the 'affected' value, which is the natural stat plus
all the bonuses from gear, spells, etc.
	n
A character's 'real' or natural values are raised with boost points,
certain skills, and possibly special quests.  Although there is no
theoritical limit to this value, there are -very- limited methods for
increasing these values.
	n
A character's 'affected' or modified values are raised with wearing of
gear, through spells, and other methods of generating bonuses for the
character.  This value has a cap or limit.
	n
The base limits for 'affected' stats:
Attributes (strength, intelligence, etc):  +8
Hitroll and Damroll:  +10
	n
These limits are modified by the character's selection of classes.  An
example of this is that a level 30 warrior would have a higher stat-cap
for strength, a level 30 wizard would have a higher stat-cap for their
intelligence score.  Assuming the level 30 warrior class-bonus for their
strength is +8, then the new 'affected' stats limit for the character
would be +16
then for a wizard it would be +16 to their intelligence.  
If you had a level 15/15 warrior/wizard, then your str and int cap would
be +12 / +12.
	n
	YSee Also:	n  STATS SCORE

