BUCK

Usage:  buck

Buck is the command that mounts use to try and get rid of an unwanted rider.

See also:  DISMOUNT MOUNT TAME
#0
AUTO-BUFF AUTOBUFF BUFF-SELF BUFFING SELF-BUFFING


Usage: buffself add (spell / power name)
       buffself remove (spell / power name)
       buffself (# psp) (spell / power name)
       buffself list
       buffself perform
       buffself cancel
 
This command allows you to create a list of spells and/or psionic
powers to buff yourself with using just a single command.
 
You set up your buff list using the buff add and buff remove commands.
Typing buff list will show you what buffs you have in your list
currently.
 
Typing buff followed by a # and a psionic power name will
allow you to assign an amount of augment psp to be used with that
power when buffing.
 
Typing buff perform will start the buffing process, and buff cancel will
end it prematurely if you desire.
 
Currently the buff system does not check if you have a spell/power
prepared, nor does it account for the quick chant feat and anything else
that will speed up spellcasting speed. The spell will simply not work
when buffing if it it not known/prepared.

#0
BUGS IDEAS TYPOS

Usage: bug submit <bug report>
       idea submit <your new idea>
       typo submit <that nasty typo>       

For making useful suggestions and reporting problems to the Powers that Be. You
must first submit a title for your report after which you will be able to enter
more detailed information if required.

Examples:

  > bug submit crash bug
  > the entire game crashes when I type 'put bag in bag'
  > /s

#0
BUILD-PLAYER-SHOP


Checklist:
  -Make sure the player has the appropriate fee either on hand or in bank
  -Make sure the player has the appropriate descriptions ready
.

You will need to create the shop-storage room and then the sales-floor, two rooms first.
Then you will build the salesman mobile, you can copy mobile 899 for appropriate
flag sets, then adjust the description.  The mobile stats/level are irrelevant.
Then you will set the salesman to load in the sales-floor via zedit, make sure it
has the <spec> flag set, inform a coder to assign the player-shop spec to the mobile.
.

Then you can use hsedit to make the shop using the house-system:
House-type: player owned
Atrium: your sales floor
Owner: put the shop owner's name here
.

Make sure to use the HSEDIT command in the room where the shop-storage is going to be.
.
Finally, add the room flag:  player-shop
.

See also: player-ran-shop
.

#0
BUILDING-RULES

	n
By Ambanya
	n
Rooms:
	n
    -Rooms may not be repeated without special exception. This includes
roads. It excludes mazes.
	n
Room Titles:
	n
    -Titles must not be repeated ad nauseum, unless it's a maze.
Differentiate each one, even for roads and similar rooms, where possible.
    -Every word in a room title must be capitalized, excepting only
determiners and prepositions, which may or may not be as befits your
preference. The first word must always be capitalized. Example: "A Long,
Dark, Road through the Marsh" may also be "A Long, Dark Road Through The
Marsh".
    -Titles should contain adjectives. Remember that most players will
only see the title in a room. Use description words wherever possible.
    -Titles may not contain the word "you." They may not contain actions
or reactions taken by the player.
	n    
Room Description:
	n
    -All rdescs must be formatted with /fi.
    -All rdescs must be longer than two lines. Two lines and a word on
the third is acceptible. The ideal rdesc is 5 or 6 lines, so aim for that.
    -All rdescs must contain at least one adjective.
    -Rdescs may not contain the word "you." They may not contain actions
or reactions taken by the player.
    -Outdoor rdescs should usually not mention weather, sounds that are
time-dependent (like things awake during the day), and other things that
are not constant for everyone standing in that spot. Exceptions are made
for quest-important rooms.
    -Rdescs may mention function of things that aren't immediately apparent
where important for setting. Builders are not limited to laundry lists of
physical objects; rather, they should use rdescs to establish setting.
	n    
Room Exits:
	n
    -The exits for NESW must have descriptions in every room. No exceptions.
    -Exit descriptions for U and D are optional, but generally recommended
where reasonable.
    -Exit descriptions may not be longer than a single line.
    -Exit descriptions should only mention activity, sounds, etc in adjacent
rooms in vague terms. Exceptions are made for quest-important rooms.
	n    
Extra descs:
	n
    -Every noun in a title, rdesc, exitdesc, or extra desc, should probably
have its own extra desc. This is not a rule, but a strong suggestion.
    -Every noun from the above rule that is particularly noticeable or
important must have an extra desc.
    -Extra descs may use "you", contain actions or reactions made by the
player, break immersion with humor, etc. The purpose is still description,
though, so be reasonable.
    -Don't be stingy with extra descs. Yes, that's a rule. Ambanya decides
if you've broken it.
	N
Mobs:
	N
   -Mobs should have at least one adjective in the name. No "a fly". It's
"an annoying, buzzing fly." The ONLY exception is named mobs.
   -mdescs may not contain the word "you" or contain actions made by the
player. General feelings are okay, like the line "A sense of dread follows
wherever the Darklord Kraal goes."
	n
