#0
CARRIAGE

There are special rooms that are carriage stations that you can travel between.
To take a carriage, type carriage <name of destination>
These rooms will be easy to identify by the room description:
This room is a carriage stop.  Use the carriage command to see options.
The menu will look like this if you do not use an argument:
Available Carriage Destinations:
Carriage Destination:          Cost   Distance Time (sec) (Area Note)
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ 
ardeep forest                    45         21         10 (level 3-12 mobs)
blindbreak rest                 105         29         14 (level 10-11 mobs, questline)
dollhouse                        65        241        120 (level 5-8 mobs, questline)
graven hollow                    70         68         34 (level 7-12 mobs, questline)
mere of dead men                110        425        212 (level 9-30 mobs)
Example, to travel to ardeep forest you would type:
carriage ardeep forest
The travel time to the destination in seconds will be determined by how far
the station is from your current location.  Travelling by carriage is completely
safe from encounters.
See Also:  SURVEY, WILDERNESS
#0
CAST CASTING IMBIBE MAGIC

Usage: cast '<spell name>' [target]
       imbibe '<extract name>'

For "magical" people.  If you want to throw a spell at someone or something.

Also for alchemists who wish to use an extract.  Note that extracts are all self only unless the alchemist has learned the infusion discovery (note: not infuse mutagen).

Example:

  > cast 'burning hands' <player>
  Note that the name of the spell must be enclosed by '.

See also: help on each individual spell:

Examples:

  > help cure-ligh
  > help fireb
  > help energy-drain


Nearly all spells require PREPARATION and will involve
CASTING-TIME to complete the spell.

	YSee Also:	n  PREPARATION CASTING-TIME SPELLS

#0
CASTING-CLASS

'Casting Class' is a term to refer to classes that deal heavily with
casting, including wizards, clerics, druids, etc.

See Also:  SPELLS
#0
CASTER-LEVEL CASTING-LEVEL

A character's caster-level is their combined levels of casting classes.  This includes
(but is not limited to) their total level as a wizard, cleric, druid, etc.  Some
classes levels don't directly count 1 for 1 in levels, such as weaker casting classes
(paladins, rangers, etc).

The casting-level will determine how powerful a caster is in some of his magics, affect
whether he can acquire certain magic-related feats, and the ability to recharge staves and
wands.

See also:  RECHARGE EPIC-SPELLS
#0
CASTING-TIME

Casting time refers to the nature of spells that can't be completed in an insant.

Generally speaking, spells as they get more powerful, take more time to cast.
This is reflected by "casting time."  If an opponent knocks you down, or somehow
breaks your CONCENTRATION while casting, you will not be able to complete the spell.

Casting time can be reduced by QUICK-CHANT.

See also:  QUICK-CHANT CASTING CONCENTRATION
