#0
CHARMEES CHARMIES FOLLOWERS

Charmee is a term coined for mobile (non-player) characters that are
either charmed, or otherwise controlled by PC (player characters).

The current follower limits are as follow:
1 Elemental
1 Undead
1 Animal Companion
1 Familiar
1 Paladin-Mount
1 Other Follower

Note: Upon copyover, death, or logging out, your charmees will disappear causing you to have to get them again.

You can recall all of your charmies to your current room by typing 'summon'.

See Also: ORDER, DISMISS, SUMMON-CHARMIES

#0
AUCTION CHAT CONGRATULATIONS GOSSIP GRATS

Usage: auction <message>
       chat <message>
       grats <message>

These are channels reserved for specific purposes.  Messages on these
channels reach everyone who is monitoring them.   
 
These channels should be used accordingly.
 
Examples:

  > auction short sword -- minimum bid 100k
  > gossip Hey, is that a short sword on your belt or are you happy to see me?
  > grats GRATS Detta!!!!!!!!

See also: TOGGLE, EMOTE, GSAY, HOLLER, NOREPEAT, SAY, SHOUT

#0
CHECKAPPROVED

Usage:  checkapproved

This command will list all the hlquests in-game that need
to be checked and approved in order to be open to the public.

See Also:  HLQUEST

#0
CHESTS LOOT LOOT-BOXES LOOT-CHESTS PILFER TREASURE-CHESTS


Usage : loot <chest keyword>
      : pilfer <chest keyword>

Special treasure chests can be found in various places around the world.
These chests are special in that they can be looted by multiple people, and
award a random item and coinage based on the level of and type of chest.
These chests can be looted once every four hours, per individual.  For those
with skill in sleight of hand, they can attempt to pilfer the chest instead of
looting it.  If successful, they can loot the chest without having to clear the
room of mobs.  Otherwise the chest can only be looted if all mobs in the room
are killed or otherwise removed from the room.

