#0
CLAN CLANS

Usage: clan

The clan command simply gives a list of clan-based commands that are avilable 
to you.

If you wish to apply to join a clan, you should look at the available choices
by typing 	yclan info	n to see a list of clans, then 	yclan info <num>	n to see more
information about a particular clan.

When you have found the clan you like, type 	yclan apply <num>	n to apply to that
clan.  You will receive a message when your application has been approved.

To start a new clan you need at least 5 members and 12 million gold coins.
You can then contact the staff to create your clan.

See Also: CLAN-INFO CLAN-APPLY

#0
CLAN-APPLICATIONS CLAN-APPLY

Usage: clan apply <clan ID>

The clan apply command is used to apply to join a clan.  You can apply to only
one clan at a time.  If you apply to a different clan, then your previous
application is cancelled.

After you have applied, the clan leader of clan admins must approve your 
application.  You will receive a message when this happens.  Your application
can only be approved while you are online.

See Also: CLAN

#0
AWARDING-CLANPOINTS CLAN-AWARD

Usage: clan award <member name> <num>

Usually reserved for clan leaders, this command allows you to award clan points
to deserving clan members.

See Also: CLAN

#0
CLAN-BALANCE

Usage: clan balance

Shows the clan's current bank balance.

See Also: CLAN-DEPOSIT CLAN-WITHDRAW

#0
CLAIMING-AREAS CLAIMING-ZONES CLAN-CLAIM

Usage: clan claim

To claim a zone, there are certain pre-requisites that you must perform.

* You clan's popularity in the zone must meet the minimum requirement.

* You must be standing in the zone you wish to claim.

Once a zone has been claimed by your clan, all members of other clans must pay
a tax on money gained from kills within that zone.  This tax is paid directly
into the clan bank, where the clan leader can spend it as they choose, such as
sharing it between their own clan members, buying a clanhall or clan eq.

See Also: CLAN POPULARITY

#0
CLAN-DEMOTE CLAN-DEMOTION

Usage: clan demote

This command is used to lower a clan member's rank by 1.

You must have access to this command, and be of a higher rank than the person
that you wish to demote.

See Also: CLAN CLAN-PROMOTE

#0
CLAN-BANK CLAN-DEPOSIT

Usage: clan deposit <amount>

Allows your hard-earned money to be donated to your clan's funds.  The clan bank
account should steadily increase as your clan claims zones, but you may have a
little excess gold to get rid of, and wish to donate it towards a clanhall or
clan eq.

Most clan members are usually able to deposit into the clan bank, but often only
clan admin and the clan leader can withdraw it.

See Also: CLAN-WITHDRAW CLAN-CLAIM

#0
CLAN-EDIT CLAN-OLC

Usage: clan edit

Clan leaders may use the clan edit command to enter a menu-based editor (OLC),
that allows several options to be changed, including all clan priveleges and 
ranks.

Imps can also use the clan editor, by specifying a clan ID number on the end of
the command.

See Also: CLAN

#0
CLAN-ENROL CLAN-ENROLMENT

Usage: clan enrol
       clan enrol <player>
       
After a player has applied to join a clan, they need their application to be
accepted by the clan's leaders.  This is done using the clan enrol command.

Typing just clan enrol will display a list of clan applicants who are currently
online.

See Also: CLAN CLAN-EXPEL

#0
CLAN-EXPEL

Usage: clan expel <player>

Boots a clan member out of the clan.  This can also be used to deny a clan 
application.

See Also: CLAN CLAN-WHO

#0
CLAN-INFO CLAN-INFORMATION

Usage: clan info
       clan info <clan ID>

Displays a list of all clans, or information about one clan.

See Also:

#0
CLAN-LIST CLAN-WHO

Usage: clan list
       clan who

Lists all members of your own clan.  Also show which clan members are online,
and their ranks.

See Also: CLAN-WHERE CLANTALK

#0
CHANGE-CLAN-OWNER CHANGING-CLAN-OWNER CLAN-OWNER

Usage: clan owner <player>

This command can only be used by the clan leader, to transfer leadership of a
clan to another person.

The new owner must be a clan member, and not an Imm.

See Also: CLAN

#0
CLAN-PROMOTE CLAN-PROMOTION

Usage: clan promote

This command is used to increase a clan member's rank by 1.

You must have access to this command, and be of a higher rank than the person
that you wish to promote.

See Also: CLAN CLAN-DEMOTE

#0
CLAN-STATUS

Usage: clan status

Displays your current clan and rank.

See Also: CLAN-INFO

#0
CLAN-WHERE

Usage: clan where

Shows the current location of all online clan members.

See Also: CLAN-WHO

#0
CLAN-WITHDRAW

Usage: clan withdraw <amount>

Withdraw gold from the clan's bank account.

See Also: CLAN-DEPOSIT

#0
CLAN-CHANNEL CLANTALK CT

Usage: clantalk <message>
       ct <message>

Send a message on the clantalk channel.  Message sent on the clantalk channel
can only be seen by other clan members and by Imms.

See Also: HISTORY

#0
CLASS-ALCHEMIST

	m-----------------------------------------------------------------	n
	m>Description:	n
	n

The alchemist's reputation is not softened by his exuberance in perfecting 
his magical extracts and potion-like creations, infusing these substances 
with magic siphoned from his aura and using his own body as experimental 
stock. Nor is it mollified by the alchemist's almost gleeful passion for 
building explosive bombs and discovering strange new poisons and methods 
for their use. These traits, while making him a liability and risk for 
most civilized organizations and institutions of higher learning, seem 
to fit quite well with most adventuring groups.
	n
	m>Class Abilities:	W Discoveries, Bombs, Mutagens
	n
	m>Alignment:     	W Any 	n
	m>Hit Dice:      	W 4-8 Per Level 	n
