CONFUSED CONFUSION

A character that is confused can result in one of the
following actions in a combat round:
20% - Act Normally
30% - Perform Nothing (stand around idly)
20% - Flee in Fear
30% - Strike a Nearby Random Target (even friendly)

#0
CONSIDER

Usage: consider [target]

This command will compare your Level with the <monsters> level.  You will then
receive a rough estimate, which is by no means exact.  Consider does not take
hitpoints/special attacks/damage into account.

Example:

  > consider chuck norris

The autoconsider toggle will show your level difference in the room view.

See also: HIT, KILL, AUTOCONSIDER
#0
CONSUMABLES STORE UNSTORE

Usage: quaff (spell name)
       recite (target) (spell name)
       use (target) (spell name)
       invoke (spell name)
       store (item name)
       store list (potions|scrolls|wands|staves)
       unstore (potion|scroll|wand|staff) (spell name)

	RNOTE:	n You must enable stored consumables with USESTOREDCONSUMABLES or
PREFEDIT to use this system. Otherwise, use the instructions in HELP USE.

Potions, Scrolls, Wands and Magical Staves are all part of the consumables
system. Instead of using physical objects, these physical items can now be
stored or unstored. This allows them to be used by referring to a spell name,
similar to casting spell, instead of trying to target the correct object in your
inventory.

By storing the item, it adds that item's spell to your relevant consumables
list, which can be seen by typing: store list (item type).  In the case of wands
and staves, it also stores the number of charges the item contains when storing.

These items may be reverted back to a physical item with the unstore command.
This allows them to be traded between players if desired.

Using a consumable requires and uses a swift action.

Note that the level at which the spell is 'cast' from using the consumable item
is set to the minimum level required to cast the spell through normal means.
The effective casting level of the item can be increased through a character's
use magic device skill.
