#0
CRAFT-BONUSES

\nUsage: craft bonuses (slot) (bonus location) (bonus type) (modifier) (specific)\n\nThis command is used to set the bonuses on an item. An item can have up\nto six bonuses. The (slot) parameter specifies which of these you would\nlike to edit. The bonus location is the name of the stat modifier, such\nas strength, dexterity, hitroll, reflex saving throw, and so forth.\nYou can see a list of these with the 'applies' command. The bonus type is\neither enhancement or universal, except for armor-class which also allows\nnatural armor and deflection bonus types. A universal bonus will stack, whereas\nother types do not stack. The modifier is the amount of the bonus applied\nto the associated stat. Specific is meant for skills, spell slots and feats.\nFor skills, this is the name of the skill the bonus is given to. For feats,\nthis is the feat name, and for spell slots it is the name of the class\nthe bonus spell slots(s) are applied to.\n\nSee Also: CRAFT\n\n

#0
CRAFT-CHECK

\nUsage: craft check\n\nThis command will say whether the crafting project is ready to start or not. If not, it\nwill list the things you are missing.\n\n

#0
CRAFT-ENHANCEMENT

\nUsage: craft enhancement (enhancement modifier)\n\nThis is only used for weapons, armor and shields. It applies an enhancement bonus\nto the item. For weapons, this enhancement bonus is applied to hitroll and damroll.\nFor armor and shield, it is applied to armor class. Note that for body, arms,\nlegs and head slots, the actual enhancement is the average of these four slots.\nNote also, that this enhancement bonus is independent of the 6 bonus slots\nan item might have.\n\nSee Also: CRAFT, CRAFT-BONUSES\n\n

#0
CRAFT-EXTRADESC CRAFT-KEYWORDS CRAFT-ROOMDESC CRAFT-SHORTDESC

Usage: craft keywords (string)\n     : craft shortdesc (string)\n     : craft roomdesc (string)\n     : craft extradesc (string)\n\nThese commands will set the various descriptions for the crafted item.\nKeywords - these are the words used to target the item with commands.\nShortdesc - this is what is displayed as the object's name.\nRoomdesc - displayed when the object is listed when one looks in a room.\nExtradesc - optional, displayed when someone looks at the item.\n

#0
CRAFT-ITEMTYPE

Usage: craft itemtype (weapon|armor|jewelry|instrument|misc)\n\nThis command will set the type of item you will create. This must be set\nbefore most other craft commands.\n\nSee Also: CRAFT\n

#0
CRAFT-MATERIALS

\nUsage: craft materials (add|remove) (material type)\n\nThis command will add or remove materials to the crafting project. To see what types\nof materials needed for the item, you need to set item type, specific type and variant\nfirst. Then typing craft show, you'll see the types of materials needed and how many.\nTo see a list of your owned materials, type materials.\n\nWhen you use the command, specifying add or remove, this will automatically add/remove\nthe exact number needed, assuming you have enough.\n\nSee Also: CRAFT\n\n

#0
CRAFT-RESET

\nUsage: craft reset\n\nThis command will reset your crafting project to default values. It will return any\nallocated materials, shards or motes in the process.\n\n

#0
CRAFT-SCORE

Usage: craft score\n\nThis command will display your crafting and harvesting skills, their rank, experience, and\nexperience required for the next rank.\n\n

#0
CRAFT-SHOW

\nUsage: craft show\n\nThis command will show the information for the current crafting project, such as\ndescriptions, item types, materials, bonuses and more.\n\nSee Also: CRAFT CRAFT-CHECK\n\n

#0
CRAFT-SPECIFIC-TYPE CRAFT-SPECIFICTYPE

Usage: craft specifictype (type)\n\nThis command will set the subtype of the item. For weapons, this is\nthe weapon type. For armor and shields, this is the specific\narmor piece. For jewelry and misc, this is the wear slot, and\nfor instruments, it's the instrument type.\n\nTyping craft specifictype by itself will display the options.\nThis require the itemtype to be set first.\n\nSee Also: CRAFT CRAFT-ITEMTYPE\n

#0
CRAFT-VARIANT

Usage: craft variant (variant name)\n\nThis command sets the variant type of the crafting type chosen.\nThis requires the item type and specific type to be set\nfirst.\n\nType craft variant will list your variant options. Most\ncraft types have more than one variant. The variant will\ndetermine the materials required to craft the item, as well\nas the keywords required in the item descriptions. For\nexample, if the item type is weapon, and the specific type\nis long sword. The variants may be long sword, broad sword,\nand war sword. If the variant is set to broad sword,\nthen the item keywords, short desc and room desc must\ncontain the phrase 'broad sword' in them. It will also\nset the material type requirements to those associated with\nthe broad sword variant.\n

#0
CHECKCRAFT CRAFTCHECK

Craftcheck is the command used in crafting, on conjunction with the
create command to check the results of a crafting attempt.  Just
follow all the steps required to CREATE an item, and instead of
typing CREATE, type 'craftcheck' to check what the results will
be.

See Also:  CREATE CRAFTING

*NOTE:  The craftcheck command has been changed to CHECKCRAFT it
otherwise functions exactly the same.
#0
CRAFTEDIT

	n
-- Craftedit Menu : [1]             	WID number	n
1) Craft Name     : <No Name>       	WThe name of this craft	n
2) Craft Timer    : 0 seconds       	WHow long to create	n
3) Craft Item     : "None"          	WThe result product (vnum)	n
4) Craft Self Msg : "You craft $p." 	WMessage for crafting item $p	n
5) Craft Room Msg : "$n crafts $p." 	WTo-room for crafting item $p	n
S) Craft Skill    : No Skill (0)    	WSkill required to create this	n
F) Flags          : None            	WSet flags here, see below	n
R) Requirements   :                 	WList of req. objs, see below	n
  None
X) Delete                           	WThis options will delete this	n
Q) Quit                             	WThis options will exit	n
	n
	WFLAGS:	n
  	c"Needs recipe"	n - does this particular craft require you have the recipe?
                   a recipe is a object of 'blueprint' type that refers to
                   the ID number of this craft
  	c--more flags to come soon!--	n
	n
	WREQUIREMENTS:	n
  Here you will enter a list of requirements to create this object, it can include
components to assemble, an in-room component(s) such as a forge, and these items
can either be destroyed or preserved depending on failure or success.  Here are
the details of the requirement-flags:
  	c"INROOM"	n - This particular requirement has to be in the room you are in, example
             is a forge
  	c"SAVEonFAIL"	n - by default if you fail the craft, you lose all the components,
                 setting this flag will preserve this particular item on FAILed craft
  	c"!REMOVE"	n - by default all the components are consumed, this particular item
              will not be consumed (fail or not)
	n
	WNotes:	n
  	c*There is no VNUM system for this crafting system, just a reference ID number.	n
  	c*You can use > show craft <name> to display info on a craft. 	n
     	cThe information varies if the craft is a RECIPE(BLUEPRINT)/NON-RECIPE(NON-BLUEPRINT)	n
  	c*Typing "craft" will bring up the crafts list for your character, and colour code	n
     	cwhich crafts you have the goods to create.	n
	n
#0
CRAFTING

The crafting system on Luminari is heavily influenced by d20MUD's system,
it was re-written by Zusuk for TBA codebase and adapted to Luminari's
game mechanics.

There are 3 primary elements to the crafting system:
Creation
Modification
Auto-Crafting Quest

Creation is done with the CREATE command.  In order to make an item, you
need a MOLD, materials, optionally an enchantment crystal and money.
You'll need to take these items and put them inside a -KIT and
use the CREATE command to make the item.

Modification includes:  AUGMENT, CONVERT, RESTRING and RESIZE.  These
crafting commands require you put the item you want to modify in the
crafting kit to be used.  Refer to the respective help files for more
details.

Auto-Crafting Quest represents local militias need for weapons, armor
and other war supplies to supplement their battle against the growing
monster presence in the world.  Refer to the SUPPLYORDER help file for
more info.

To see your crafting proficiency, just type 	YPRAC	n

See Also:  AUGMENT CONVERT RESTRING SUPPLYORDER RESIZE CRAFTCHECK
            CREATE -KIT AUTOCRAFT DISENCHANT


See Also:
http://www.luminarimud.com/forums/topic/crafting-101-2018/

Special thanks to the author, Ellyanor for the contribution!
#0
CRAFTING-KIT CRAFTINGKIT

Crafting Kit is an item required to do the crafting commands.  Just
put the required items in the kit and type in the appropriate command.

All new players are now starting with a free crafting-kit.

See Also:  CRAFTING
#0
CRAFTING-MOTES MOTES

\n   Motes are used in crafting projects to add magical bonuses to the crafted\nitems.  Each mote type has associated bonus types it can affect, and the greater\nthe bonus, the greater the number of motes are required to enchant the item so.\n\n\nYou can see which bonuses are associated with which mote type, by using the \tYmotes\tn\ncommand\n\n

#0
CRAFTS

There is a system of special crafting that includes a universal list of
special objects AND objects that are available through rare recipes.

Usage: craft <no argument> - View all known crafts based on skill
craft <name of object from list or blueprint> - If you have the required
items, start crafting it

See also:  crafting, checkcraft, crafting-kit

#0
CRASHES

A crash is when the game decides to reboot itself, without the benefit of 
letting us know in advance.

See also: REBOOT
#0
CREATE

The create command is used in crafting system to create new gear.  In
order to create new gear you'll need to follow these steps:

1)  You will need a CRAFTING-KIT
2)  You will need to buy/find a MOLD with the design you want
3)  You will need to buy/find the MATERIAL you need for the design
    (You can look at the MOLD to see what MATERIAL you need)
4)  Optionally you need to add a CRYSTAL to help enhance the item
5)  Throw all the items in your CRAFTING-KIT
6)  Then type:  create <new item name>

See Also:  CRAFTING-KIT MATERIAL MOLD CRYSTAL
