#0
DEATH

\n Death is a normal part of gameplay, and should not be seen as a major obstacle.\nWhen your character dies, the only thing you will lose is some experience\npoints. You will be sent to the MUD's start room where you can safely heal and\nprepare for upcoming encounters. \n \nIf you die while working on a quest encounter, or trying to defeat a difficult\nNPC, it may be helpful to try one of the following before attempting the\nencounter again:\n \n \tc1.\tn Find some help - try asking for help from other players online, as well as\non our Discord channel.\n \n \tc2.\tn Level up - Try gaining a level or two before trying it up. You can see what\nareas in the game are appropriate for your level with the 'areas' command. You\ncan also use 'areas all' as well as 'areas (level start) (level end). Eg.\n'areas 10 15' will show all zones that fall within the 10 to 15 level range.\nYou can get to these areas a number of ways, such as by sailing, taking a\ncarriage, asking other players, or using the 'landmarks' and 'walkto' commands.\n \n \tc3.\tn Try to upgrade your gear - Start by going to areas in your level range. Many\nmobs drop useful gear, not just boss-mobs. You can also use our online object\ndatabase at https://krynn.d20mud.com/objectdb/ or you can try your hand at\ncrafting, which is useful right from level one, with instructions at\nhttps://krynn.d20mud.com/wiki/crafting/ In addition to these methods, you can\ndo bounties for quest points and spend your quest points in the bazaar. Bounty\ngivers and bazaars can be found in Palanthas and Sanction. Finally you can ask\nother players if they have gear they're willing to sell or give away. Palanthas\nand Sanction also have donation rooms, though their contents are erased with\neach server restart, so this is not dependable.\n \tn\nIf you still cannot have success with these steps, please speak with a staff\nmember. We'll review the encounter for appropriate difficulty, and will address\nit if we feel it's more difficult than it should be. However, if the builder\nintended the fight to be higher difficulty, and the reward is commensurate, we\nmay not alter the encounter.\n \tn\nAbove all, if you die, don't get discouraged! We are here to help, and want to\nsee you enjoy your time here. Always feel free to contact staff with concerns\nor questions.\n

