#0
DETECT-TRAP DETECTTRAP


Usage: detecttrap [object]

This command will use your skill in 'perception' to try and find
any traps in your immediate area. With an object argument, it examines an
object in your inventory or in the room for a converted Realms of Luminari
object trap. Object traps may trigger when moved past, picked up, put into a
container, opened, or picked, depending on how the trap was configured.

Once you have detected a room trap, you must 	Rdisabletrap	n in the same room
to disarm it. Converted object traps can be disabled by naming the object;
as in the source game, object disarming does not require a remembered
detection state.

	YSee Also:	n PERCEPTION DISABLETRAP

#0
DEVELOPMENT

Development

CHECKOUT from svn, /home/luminari/svn/luminari/ the code so you have a local copy
svn+ssh://luminarimud.com/home/luminari/svn/luminari
write new code
compile locally to check for obvious errors
UPDATE to make sure you are not creating conflicts
fix any conflicts
COMMIT your code to the subversion
type ./qupdate.sh to checkout/compile development port 4001, directory tba/
test changes thoroughly on test port
in-game on primary port 4100, report what was done to the code: change <whatever you did>
now you have the choice of just moving the code over to product: ./qupdate_luminari.sh
or you can run the big script which backs everything up, and does other clean up (longer)
  ./update_luminari.sh
Do not forget to add a helpfile if appropriate via HEDIT

Recommended:  running ./update_luminari.sh at least once a week and adding a website post


NOTE: the developers are all working off trunk, there are ambitions of implementing a proper
system for branches and merging, but we wanted to change revision systems before-hand.
If you are interested in helping make this change, please let the lead developer know.

