#0
DISABLE-TRAP DISABLETRAP


Usage: disabletrap [object]

The disable trap command will use your 'disable device' skill to
attempt to disarm a trap you just found in the room you are in.
You will not be able to disable a trap unless you have first
detected it by using 	Rdetecttrap	n command.

With an object argument, the command attempts to disarm a converted Realms
of Luminari object trap in your inventory or in the room. A failed object
attempt can trigger the trap. A successful attempt reduces its charges to
zero and persists with the object.

If you fail your skill check by 5 or more you will set off the
trap and suffer the consequences of tripping the trap normally.

	YSee Also:	n DETECTTRAP DISABLE-DEVICE

#0
DISARM

You can attempt to disarm your opponent in place of a melee attack. If you
do not have the Improved Disarm feat, or a similar ability, attempting to
disarm a foe provokes an attack of opportunity from the target of your
maneuver. Attempting to disarm a foe while unarmed imposes a 4 penalty on
the attack.

If your attack is successful, your target drops one item it is carrying, in
this order: wielded two-handed, wielded primary hand, wielded off hand.
If your attack fails by 10 or more, you drop the weapon that you were using
to attempt the disarm.

It is important to note that attempting to pick up an item during combat
will use a move-action

See Also:  IMPROVED-DISARM
#0
DISBAND-GROUP


   In order to disband a group you can either 'group leave' or 'group kick' (if
you're the group leader).  In order to get rid of any charmies you might have,
you should type 'summon' to bring them all to you, and then use the 'dismiss'
command on each charmie.

#0
DISCIPLINE

Usage:  Automatic

Prereq:  None

Discipline is your ability to resist combat feats, each point invested in discipline
reflects a percentage point resistance against the combat feats.

So far Discipline can provide defense against the following skills:
Bash
Improved Bash
Trip
Improved Trip
Kick

See also:  BASH TRIP KICK
#0
DISCLAIMER

   All areas submitted or created on LuminariMUD will remain the property
of the original builder.  By creating or submitting an area the builder gives 
the staff of Luminari the right to edit, modify, and use the material as we see fit 
on Luminari without any penalty, fee, whining, or obligation of any sort.  Luminari
staff will not normally modify anyone's work. However, it is sometimes necessary for 
troubleshooting, fixing errors, or game balance.
   A builder can request a copy of their work from us at any time.  A builder's
work will not leave Luminari without their explicit permission.  The builder will 
always be given public credit for their work. If a builder abandons their work 
without notifying us, they may be deleted and their work will either be deleted or
donated depending on the quality.

#0
DISEASE

The diseased affect means the character's health is weakened
from sickness.  Currently disease prevents the victim's health
from ever getting above 60% of maximum value.

See Also:  POISON SPELLS
#0
DISENCHANT

Disenchant takes the magical essence of items and through
a special process, extracts some of the power into a
special crafting essence.

Any item that is "magical" is disenchantable.

See Also:  CRAFTING
#0
DISENGAGE

Usage:  disengage

Disengage is a combat command allowing you to stop fighting
the current target you are engaged with as long as you are
not 'tanking' the target.

See Also:  TANKING

