DONATE DONATING DONATION

Usage: donate <object>
       donate <number> coins

This command takes an object that you no longer want and deposits it in one of
the MUDs donation rooms.

  > donate shield
  > donate all.bread
  > donate 500 coins

See also: JUNK, GET
#0
DOWNGRADE DOWNGRADING-ITEMS

Usage: downgrade (object) (new level) (optional confirmation code)\n\nThe downgrade command will allow you to take a higher level item\nand reduce it to a lower level.\n\nSome things to note:\n-- An item can only ever be downgraded once.\n-- An item must be identified to downgrade. A lore check will automatically\n   be attempted when you downgrade. If it fails, you will need to\n   get someone else to lore check it, or use an identify spell\n   to identify it before you can downgrade it.\n-- An item must be downgraded to a level lower than the current item level.\n-- Any weapon spells, special abilities, permananet affects or activated spells,\n   are removed from the item.\n-- The enhancement bonus and any other bonuses will be reduced\n   by an amount dependant on the difference between the original\n   item level and the new item level. If the difference is too\n   great, some bonuses may be removed altogether.\n-- The downgrade will cost an amount in gold equal to the\n   item's original level * 50.\n\nWhen you type in the downgrade command: downgrade (obj) (level),\nYou will be shown the stats of the new item and a confirmation\ncode. To proceed with the downgrade you must repeat\nthe downgrade command and add the confirmation code at\nthe end.\n\n

#0
DRAC-BREATH DRACBREATH DRACONIC-BREATH

This ability, unique to Sorcerers with the Draconic Bloodline, grants
the Sorcerer a breath weapon based on the type of Dragon selected for
their Bloodline.  This breath weapon deals 1d6 damage per Sorcerer level
of the appropriate Draconic Bloodlines energy type.

Usage: dracbreath <target>
#0
DRAC-CLAWS DRACCLAWS DRACONIC-CLAWS

This ability, unique to Sorcerers with the Draconic Bloodline, allows
the Sorcerer to call upon their lineage and grow magical claws to make attacks.
These claw attacks deal a base of 1d4 + strength each.  These attacks
at level 7 will also bypass DR/magic.  At level 9 the base damage
increases to 1d6 + strength and bypasses DR/magic.  Finally, at level 11
these claw attacks will deal 1d6 + strength, bypass DR/magic and do an 
additional 1d6 points of energy damage based upon the Sorcerers Draconic Bloodline.

Usage: dracclaws
#0
DRACONIC-BLOODLINE DRACONIC-HERITAGE

Sorcerers have the option to select a bloodline that explains where their
magical prowess comes from.  In the case of draconic bloodline, the sorcerer
has partial draconic ancestry, and as a result, as they grow in prowess
some of that ancestry becomes manifest in enhanced abilities and even
new dragon like abilities.

Each draconic heritage is associated with a specific dragon type,
chosen when selecting the bloodline through the study menu as a
sorcerer.  This heritage will determine the energy type associated
with your draconic abilities, and the colour of your draconic wings
once acquired.

NEW CLASS SKILL: Perception

BONUS SPELLS: mage armor (3rd), resist energy (5th), fly (7th), wizard eye (9th), 
telekineses (11th), true seeing (13th), waves of exhaustion (15th), mass 
domination (17th), polymorph (19th).

CLASS FEATS: Blind Fight, Great Fortitude, Improved Initiative, 
Power Attack, Quicken Spell, Skill Focus, Toughness.

The draconic bloodline also gives the following bonus abilities:
Draconic Arcana (HELP DRACONIC ARCANA)
Draconic Claws (HELP DRACONIC CLAWS)
Draconic Resistances (HELP DRACONIC RESISTANCES)
Draconic Breath Weapon (HELP DRACONIC BREATH WEAPON)
Draconic Wings (HELP DRACONIC WINGS)
Power of Wyrms (HELP POWER OF WYRMS)


See Also: SORCERER
#0
DRAC-WINGS DRACONIC-WINGS DRACWINGS

This ability, unique to Sorcerers with the Draconic Bloodline, allows
the Sorcerer to call upon their heritage and sprout wings.  This ability
grants the Sorcerer the power of Flight.

Usage: dracwings

SEE ALSO: fly
#0
DRAGON-BOND-TYPES DRAGON-BONDS

\nDragon bonds are a more specific way in which dragon riders can bond with their\ndragon mounts. The ability is gained at dragon rider level 3, and offers the following\noptions:\n\nDragon Champion\nDragon Scion\nDragon Kin\n\nFor more information on each, see their respective help file. Ie. HELP DRAGON CHAMPION\n\n

#0
DRAGON-CHAMPION

\nLevel 3: +1 hitroll and +2 damroll when riding dragon mount.\nLevel 7: 10% reisist to piercing, slashing and bludgeoning damage when riding dragon mount.\nLevel 10: Weapon base damage (XdY) doubled when riding dragon mount.\n\nSee Also: DRAGON BOND, DRAGON SCION, DRAGON KIN\n\n

#0
DRAGON-KIN

\nLevel 3: Armor class increases by 2 when riding dragon mount.\nLevel 7: Can spend a dragoon point to give allies +2 to hitroll and 5d6 to maximum hit points.\nLevel 10: Charging while riding dragon mount has a chance to knock enemy prone and charge damage increases by 10.\n\nSee Also: DRAGON BOND, DRAGON SCION, DRAGON CHAMPION\n\n

#0
DRAGON-MAGE DRAGON-SCION

\nLevel 3: Melee attacks gain elemental damage based on dragon mount type, when riding dragon mount.\nLevel 7: Number of Dragoon points are doubled.\nLevel 10: Can sacrifice hit points to restore spell slots.\n\nSee Also: DRAGON BOND, DRAGON KIN, DRAGON CHAMPION\n\n

