	G>Description:	n
	n
Cruel and cunning, Drow, also known as dark elves, were cursed
into their present appearance by the Arcanite and Prisoner's magic, were led
down the path to evil and corruption. The drow have black skin that resembles
polished obsidian and stark white or pale yellow hair. They commonly have red
eyes. Drow are the same size as elves but a bit thinner. 
	n
Descending into the Underworld, they formed cities shaped from the rock of
cyclopean caverns. They developed a theocratic and matriarchal society based
on power and deceit. Females generally hold all positions of power and
responsibility in the government, the military, and the home. In such a society
males are often trained as warriors to become soldiers, guards, and servants of
females. Those males showing aptitude with magic are trained as Wizards instead.
While they are not born evil, malignancy is deep-rooted in their culture and
society, and nonconformists rarely survive for long.
	n
Note: Drow are an "advanced" race and therefore have a lot
more challenging experience-chart. Type 'levels' in-game to view.
	n
	G>Racial Abilities:	n
	n
	RDay Blindness: -1 penalty to hitroll, damage, saves and skills in daylight	n
	WElven Innates:  Drow have all the same innates elves do	n
	WSpell Like Abilities (SLA):  faerie fire, darkness and levitate	n
	n
	G>Ability Adjustments:  	W Int +4 Wis +2 Dex +2 Cha +2
	n
	G>Experience Modifier:  	W Double 	n
	n
	YSee Also:	n  RACES
	n
#0
CLASS-DRUID DRUID

	m-----------------------------------------------------------------	n
	m>Description:	n
	n
Druids gain power not by ruling nature, but by being at one with it.
Druids hate the unnatural, including abberations or undead, and try to
destroy them where possible.  Druids receive divine spells directly
from the natural forces of nature that the One G-d created, not the
gods, and can gain an array of powers as they gain more experience,
including the ability to take the shape of animals.  A druid is often
accompanied by an animal companion.  The weapons and armor of a druid
are restricted by their traditional oaths, not simply training.  A
druid's wisdom score should be high, as this determines the maximum
spell level that they can cast.
	n
	m>Class Abilities:	n
	n
	WShapechange	n  
	WDivine Casting	n
	WAnimal Companion	n
