#0
EFREETI EFREETI-MAGIC EFREETIMAGIC IFREETI


Usage: wildshape efreeti
     : efreetimagic (target) (detect-magic|produce-flame|scorching-ray)
     : efreetimagic (target) (invisiblity|wall-of-fire|mirror-image)
     : efreetimagic (target) (enlarge-person|reduce-person)

The efreet (singular efreeti) are genies from the Plane of Fire. An efreeti
stands about 12 feet tall and weighs about 2,000 pounds. Efreet have few
allies among geniekind. They certainly hate djinn, and attack them on sight.
They hold an equally strong enmity for marids, and view the jann as frail
and weak. Efreet often work closely with shaitans, yet even then alliances
are temporary at best.

The Efreeti is a wild shape option for members of the shifter prestige class.
Efreet are able to see in the dark, fly, and use innate efreeti magic, which includes
detect magic, produce flame, and scorching ray at will, and invisibility, wall of fire,
mirror image, enlarge person and reduce person up to 8 times per day combined.
They are surrounded by an aura of flame that deals 1d6 damage anytime a melee
attack is attempted against them.  They also deal 1d6 fire damage on any successful
melee attack of their own.
#0
ELDRITCH

Usage: eldritch shapes
       eldritch essences
       eldritch (shape or essence name)
 
The eldritch command is an easy way to manage your eldritch blast shapes and
essences. You can use the 'eldritch essences' and 'eldritch shapes' commands
to see what shapes/essences you know, and which one is active, where applicable.
 
You can toggle them on and off by typing: 'eldritch (shape/essence name)'. For
example, typing: 'eldritch hideous blow' would toggle my hideous blow eldritch
shape on or off.

	YSee Also:	n ELDRITCH BLAST
#0
AUTOBLAST BLAST ELDRITCH-BLAST

	D>Usage:           	W blast (target)	n
	D>Accumulative:    	W  	n
	D>Duration:        	W  	n
	D>School of Magic: 	W Conjuration 	n
	D>Target(s):       	W Single Target 	n
	D>Magic Resist:    	W Yes 	n
	D>Saving Throw:    	W  	n
	D>Damage Type:     	W  	n
	D>Description:	n
	n
	nEldritch blast is a warlock's most useful natural ability. Eldritch blast is
	ntreated as a crit-able ranged touch attack (and as such, your Dexterity factors
	ninto the AB). It is also a spell-like ability, and as such metamagic and spells
	nthat would normally affect a spell will not interact with eldritch blast (like
	nspell mantle).

By default, eldritch blast has no specific type and has no
	nsaving throw (but spell resistance applies), and has an effective caster level
	n(ECL) of 1. Eldritch essence & blast shape invocations will modify the effects
	nof the blast. This usually increases the ECL. If it has an additional effect
	nthat applies a save, your Charisma modifier will be applied to the
	nDC.

Gaining levels in warlock will improve the number of dice rolled with
	neldritch blast. Once eldritch blast reaches 10d6 it will bypass spell resistance
	nchecks entirely.

Use AUTOBLAST to toggle automatic eldritch blasts in place of normal attacks.
The command reports whether automatic blasting is now enabled or disabled.



	n
	n
	n
	YSee also:	n WARLOCK
	n
