#0
: EMOTES EMOTIONS TEMOTES

EMOTES
      
Usage: emote (message)
        temote (target) (message)
       
The emote system allows you to create custom messages that will echo to others
in the room.
       
The emote command allows you to add a message that follows your name.
Eg. If Gicker typed: emote is having a great day.
Shows: Gicker is having a great day.
       
The temote command does the same, however it requires a target chracter or mob
as well as a message.
Eg. If Gicker typed: temote caide Looking#M up and down,#n gives#N a suspicious glance.
Shows: Looking him up and down, Gicker gives Caide a suspicious glance.
       
Some of the emote commands allow for variables.  They are as follows:
  #n : The name or short description of the player/mob typing the emote.
  #m : Him/Her for the player/mob typing the emote.
  #e : He/She for the player/mob typing the emote.
  #s : His/her for the player/mob typing the emote.
  #N : The name or short description of the target player/mob.
  #M : Him/Her for the target player/mob.
  #E : He/She for the target player/mob.
  #S : His/her for the target player/mob.
      
