#0
GUI GUIMODE MUDLET

GUI Mudlet
---
Typing 'gui' will turn off and on "GUI Mode".
GUI Mode is part of our Mudlet GUI system.
Mudlet is an open source popular MUD client that allows the community to build 
customized interfaces for their MUDs.
LuminariMUD has a custom interface we created for Mudlet that is open-source
and may help enhance your gameplay experience.
---
A Quick tour and both video and text instructions for installing
the entire system are here:
  https://bit.ly/gui_tutorial
You can always find the latest test and release packages in this
GitHub directory:
  https://bit.ly/luminari_gui
---
*Quick note:  If in Mudlet you try opening one of the pop-up windows
such as the 'Triggers' window and you can't see it:
  Hover over the Mudlet icon in your app bar, you should be able to see
the missing window there.  Over over it, then right-click, then select
'maximize'.
---
Current GUI Commands:
- Chat & Display Commands
"gag chat" - Toggles whether chat messages are removed from the main window
    - When enabled, chat only appears in the tabbed chat window
    - When disabled, chat appears in both main window and chat tabs
"show self" - Toggles whether you appear in the Group tab
    - Useful for cleaner group display when you don't need to see your own stats
"dblink" - Toggles tab blinking for new chat messages
    - Temporary toggle that resets when GUI reloads
    - Useful if blinking is distracting
"hscroll" - Toggles horizontal scroll bar on main window
    - Helps with wide content display
- GUI Repair Commands
"fix gui" - Comprehensive fix for all GUI components
    - Re-registers all event handlers
    - Re-initializes chat system if needed
    - Refreshes all displays (Group, Player, Gauges, ASCII map)
    - Refreshes all Adjustable Containers
    - Use this when GUI stops updating properly
"fix chat" - Specific fix for chat positioning issues
    - Brings chat to front
    - Shows all chat tabs
    - Fixes display problems after package reload
- Mudlet Mapping Commands
"start mapping" - Enables automatic room mapping
"stop mapping" - Disables automatic room mapping
---
See Also:  MAP
---
#0
GULLY-DWARF RACE-GULLY-DWARF

\tG>Description:\tn
\n\tn
\n\tnThe Aghar ('Anguished'), or gully dwarves as most races call them,
\n\tnare a misbegotten race of tough survivors. Though gully dwarves themselves have
\n\tnan extensive oral tradition (they love telling stories), no two gully dwarf
\n\tnclans ever agree on the exact details of their origins or history. The commonly
\n\tnaccepted tale of how gully dwarves came to be is found within the annals of
\n\tnAstinus's Iconochronos. According to the Iconochronos, gully dwarves are the
\n\tnresult of breeding between gnomes and dwarves in the years following the
\n\tntransformation of the gnomes by the Graygem of Gargath. The gnome-dwarf
\n\tnhalf-breeds appeared to inherit the worst qualities of both races. The
\n\tnunfortunate half-breeds were driven out of their clans. Humans later christened
\n\tnthem 'gully dwarves,' reflecting their lowly status and poor living conditions. 
\n\tn
\n\tG>Racial Abilities:\tn
\n\tn
\n\tWUltravision:\tn           - Can see in the dark.
\n\tWPoison Resist:\tn         - +2 to saves vs. poison.
\n\tWStability:\tn             - +2 to bash and trip maneuver checks.
\n\tWHardiness:\tn             - +2 to saves vs. damaging spells.
\n\tWSurvival Instinct:\tn     - +3 to stealth and nature skills, Can scrounge room for supplies.
\n\tWPitiable:\tn              - 75% chance to bypass an aggressive attack by a mob.
\n\tWCowardly:\tn              - -4 to intimidate resistance, immune to taunts, can flee regardless 
\n\tn                         of movement speed and no move action needed to flee
\n\tWGrubby:\tn                - -6 to persuasion and appraise checks. 50% damage resist against poison,
\n\tn                         disease and water damage, and +4 to save dc's against disease affects.
\n\tn
\n\tG>Ability Adjustments:  \tW +4 Con, +4 Dex, -4 Int, -4 Cha  \tn
\n\tn
\n\tG>Experience Modifier:  \tW None \tn
\n\tn
\n\tYSee also:\tn RACES
\n\tn
\n

#0
HALF-ELF RACE-HALF-ELF RACE-HALFELF

	G>Description:	n
	n
	n
 Half-elves, as usually defined, were humanoids born through the
union of an elf and a human. Whether a half-elf was raised by their human parent
or their elven parent, they often felt isolated and alone. Because they took
around twenty years to reach adulthood, they matured quickly when raised by
elves (who think they look like humans), making them feel like an outsider in
either place. Most half-elves were descended from moon elves. Pairings of elves
and other races also existed, though they were rare. Half elves stood roughly
around 5 feet 5 inches to six feet two inches (1.65 - 1.88 meters), making them
only slightly shorter overall than humans, and weighed in at 130 - 190 lbs. (59
- 86 kg), making them heavier than elves but still considerably lighter than
humans. Like humans, half-elves had a wide variety of complexions, some of which
were inherited from the elven half of their heritage, such as a tendency for
metallic-hued skin and inhuman hair colors. Unlike true Tel'Quessir, however,
male half-elves were capable of growing facial hair and often did so to
distinguish themselves, in part, from their elven parents. Half-elven ears were
about the size of human ones, but like elves, they were pointed on the ends.
Half-elves were also notably more durable and passionate than either elves or
humans, a unique result of the two races' blending. 
	n
	G>Racial Abilities:	n
	n
	WInfravision:	n             - Can detect life forms in the dark.
	WHalf Blood:	n              - +2 to discipline and lore skills.
	WAdaptability:	n            - 20 percent chance per skill check for +3 bonus, and 5% bonus to all exp gains.
	WEnchantment Resistance:	n  - +2 to saves vs. enchantment.
	WKeen Senses:	n             - +2 to perception and sense motive skills.
	WSleep immunity:	n          - Immune to sleep based enchantments.
	WElven Weapons:	n           - Proficient in long swords, rapiers and all types of bows.
	n
	G>Ability Adjustments:  	W +2 Cha and 2 extra stat points when choosing ability scores 	n
	n
	G>Experience Modifier:  	W None 	n
	n
	YSee also:	n RACES
	n
#0
HALF-ORC RACE-HALF-ORC RACE-HALFORC

	G-----------------------------------------------------------------	n
	G>Description:	n
	n
Half-orcs are the short-tempered and sullen result of human and orc
pairings.  They would rather act than ponder and would rather fight
than argue.  They love simple pleasures, such as feasting, boasting
and wild dancing.  They are an asset at the right sort of party, but 
not at the duchess's grand ball.  Half-orcs are as tall as humans but
their brutish features betray their lineage.  They also regard scars as
tokens of pride and things of beauty.  They rarely reach 75 years old.
	n
	G>Racial Abilities:	n
	n
	WUltravision	n          - Can see in the dark.
	WSavage Attacks	n       - Critical hits add 1d6 damage.
	WRelentless endurance	n - 25 percent chance to avoid a killing blow.
	WMenacing	n             - +3 to intimidate checks.
	n
	G>Ability Adjustments:  	W +2 Str, +1 Con 	n
	n
	G>Experience Modifier:  	W None 	n
	n
	YSee also:	n RACES
	n
#0
HALFLING RACE-HALFLING

	G-----------------------------------------------------------------	n
	G>Description:	n
	n
Halflings are clever, capable and resourceful survivors.  They are
notoriously curious and show a daring that many larger people can't
match.  They can be lured by wealth but tend to spend rather than
hoard.  Halflings have ruddy skin, hair that is black and straight,
and brown or black eyes.  Halfling men often grow long sideburns but
rarely beards or mustaches.  They prefer practical clothing and would
rather wear a comfortable shirt than jewelry.  Haflings stand about 3
feet tall, and commonly live to see 150.
	n
	G>Racial Abilities:	n
	n
	WInfravision	n  
	WCombat Training Versus Giants:	n  +1 size bonus versus larger foes
	WShadow Hopper:	n  +2 to sneak and hide
	WLucky:	n  +1 to all saves
	n
	G>Ability Adjustments:  	W +2 Dex, -2 Str
	n
	G>Experience Modifier:  	W None 	n
	n
	YSee also:	n RACES
	n
