#0
HILL-DWARF RACE-HILL-DWARF

\tG>Description:\tn
\n\tn
\n\tnHill dwarves have left their underground halls to practice their
\n\tnskills in the greater world. Hill dwarves share the traits of their mountain
\n\tndwarf cousins, but are a bit more accepting of other races and cultures. All
\n\tnhill dwarves are of the Neidar ("Nearest") clan. A longstanding, bitter feud
\n\tnexists between hill dwarves and mountain dwarves, dating back to the Cataclysm.
\n\tnThe hill dwarves accuse the mountain dwarves of having shut the doors of
\n\tnThorbardin on them when the Neidar sought refuge following the Cataclysm. In
\n\tntheir defense, the mountain dwarves claim that they had resources enough to feed
\n\tnonly their own people and that, if they allowed the hill dwarves into the
\n\tnmountain, they all might have starved. 
\n\tn
\n\tG>Racial Abilities:\tn
\n\tn
\n\tWUltravision:\tn           - Can see in the dark.
\n\tWPoison Resist:\tn         - +2 to saves vs. poison.
\n\tWStability:\tn             - +2 to bash and trip maneuver checks.
\n\tWHardiness:\tn             - +2 to saves vs. damaging spells.
\n\tWCombat vs Giants:\tn      - +1 to attacks against large or larger opponents.
\n\tWDwarven Weapons:\tn       - Proficient in battle axe, war axe, warhammer, light hammer, light & heavy picks & urgosh.
\n\tWEncumbered Resilience:\tn - Strength is treated as 2 points higher in determining carry weight limits.
\n\tWHill Dwarf Toughness:\tn  - +1 hit point per level.
\n\tn
\n\tG>Ability Adjustments:  \tW +2 Con, +1 Wis  \tn
\n\tn
\n\tG>Experience Modifier:  \tW None \tn
\n\tn
\n\tYSee also:\tn RACES
\n\tn
\n

