HINDEX

USAGE: hindex < letter | phrase >

  The help index command is a quick reference to help keywords matching the argument
you provide. For Example:

> hindex new
Help index entries based on 'new':
newbie-policy       newbies             news          

#0
HINT NO-HINT NOHINT

The hint system is useful to all players, with emphasis on new ones.  It will
give you helpful info about various aspects about the game, lore, and community.
To turn off hints:  type nohint, or use 'prefedit' menu

#0
HISTORY

Usage: history < all | say | gossip | wiznet | tell | shout | grats | holler | auction >

   This command displays what has been said over the channel you input along
with a time stamp for when it was sent. History all will list the history of
all channels.

See also: CHANNELS, MUD-
#0
HISTORY-SKILL SKILL-HISTORY

   The history skill is mainly a role playing skill, and does not govern any\nin-game mechanics at this time.  It is a measure of a person's knowledge about\nworld history, the major players, cities, nations and so forth.\n

