#0
HITROLL

   A bonus added to your armor and weapons that increases your chances of 
hitting a creature while in battle. This does not affect how hard you hit, 
just how often.
   A player at level fifteen with a Hitroll of +25 will hit a creature more
often than a level fifteen player would with a Hitroll of +10.

See also: DAMROLL, AC, STATS, DAMAGE
#0
HLQEDIT

	n
Usage:  hlqedit <quest mobile vnum>
	n
Homeland-Quest-System (hlqedit)
	n
The hl-quest system is different then autoquest (qedit) in that it
is directly attached to the quest-mobile being used for the quest,
so the vnum will always be the same vnum as the quest-mobile. Type
hlqedit <mobile vnum> to create or modify current quests and check
out the help file:  	RHELP -MENU	n
	n
If you want information on the primary quest system (	RAUTOQUEST	n
and 	RQEDIT	n) check the respective help files.
	n
	YSee Also:	n  -MENU AUTOQUEST QEDIT
	n
#0
HLQEDIT-APPROVE

Without prior approval, no quests will function for non-staff
characters.  To get approval, just have the head-builder or a
forger check to make sure the quest is appropriate.  They will
be checking for two things:  1)  appropriate content for the
game world and 2)  an appropriate award-to-difficulty ratio for
the quest reward.

	YSee Also:	n  HLQEDIT-MENU

#0
HLQEDIT-ASK

	n
The '	Yask quest	n' option for quest-in (quest entries) is the
primary driver for getting more info from this quest-mobile.  The
information can be about anything, but most commonly, this quest-in
option is used for the quest-mobile to instruct the player how to
proceed on the quest-mobile's other quests (either 	RHLQEDIT-GIVE	n or 
	RHLQEDIT-ROOM	n).  Upon selection of this option you will be prompted
to enter a list of keywords, separate each keyword with a space:
	n
hi hello quest
	n
This list of keywords would fire the 	RHLQEDIT-DIALOGUE	n if any of those
three words is asked to the quest-mobile.
	n
After you finish your keyword list, you will be prompted to enter the
	RHLQEDIT-DIALOGUE	n for response.  You can use $N and other 	RDOLLAR-CODES	n
to help make the dialogue clear to the player.
	n
	YSee Also:	n HLQEDIT-DIALOGUE HLQEDIT-QUEST-OUT
	n
#0
HLQEDIT-ATTACK-QUESTOR

	n
The '	Yattack-questor	n' quest-reward is not much of a
reward at all.  This will cause the quest-mobile to engage
the questor in combat.
	n
When you select this option, you will be sent straight to
the 	RHLQEDIT-DIALOGUE	n to finalize the quest.
	n
	YSee Also:	n HLQEDIT-QUEST-OUT HLQEDIT
	n
#0
HLQEDIT-CAST-SPELL

	n
This quest-out option will have the quest-mobile cast on
the questor a specific question.  There is no casting time
on this spell.
	n
After filling out this quest-reward, you can continue
filling out more quest rewards if you wish via the menu
(	RHLQEDIT-QUEST-OUT	n).
	n
	YSee Also:	n HLQEDIT-QUEST-OUT HLQEDIT
	n
#0
HLQEDIT-COINS

	n
	YHomeland Quest Coins Reward	n
	n
This works very straightforward in giving a coin reward, the
upper limit for coin rewards per instance is 100,000 coins.
Selecting this reward will allow the option of giving other
rewards in adition (you will be returned to the reward menu
	RHLQEDIT-QUEST-OUT	n) to the coins.
	n
	YHomeland Quest Item Reward	n
This reward is also very straightforward, if for any reason
the quest-mobile can't successfully give the item to the
player, the item will be dropped to the ground (example would
be a !DROP cursed item).
Selecting this reward will allow the option of giving other
rewards in adition (you will be returned to the reward menu
	RHLQEDIT-QUEST-OUT	n) to the item.
	n
	YSee Also:	n HLQEDIT-QUEST-OUT HLQEDIT
	n
#0
HLQEDIT-DELETE

	n
This option will do exactly as it says, it will prompt you
to enter the quest number, as listed in the HLQEDIT-MENU
example, you could choose either 1 or 2.
	n
An important note is that once a quest is made, it can't be
editted, if you want to change it, it has to be deleted and
remade from scratch.  So it is wise to write out your quest
dialogue on Notepad/Wordpad or paper in case you want to
adjust a quest at a later time or if you make a mistake while
making the quest.
	n
	YSee Also:	n  HLQEDIT-MENU HLQEDIT-NEW
	n
#0
HLQEDIT-FOLLOW-QUESTOR

	n
This special quest-out will get the quest-mobile to start
following the questor.  It is best used in conjuction with
the quest-in command 'Room-Quests' to as to lead the quest-
mobile to a given destination and reward the player upon
accomplishing this goal.
	n
After filling out this quest-reward, you can continue
filling out more quest rewards if you wish via the menu
(	RHLQEDIT-QUEST-OUT	n).
	n
	YSee Also:	n HLQEDIT-QUEST-OUT HLQEDIT
	n
#0
HLQEDIT-GIVE

	n
When you select the quest-in (quest entry) option of 'Give' you 
will see this:
	n
C) Give Coins to Mob     	RHELP -COINS	n
I) Give Item to Mob      	RHELP -ITEM	n
Enter choice (0 to end/quit) : 
	n
After you fill out each entry, the system will return you to this
menu in case you want to add more entries for the quest.  If you
wanted the quest requirement to be two items and 100 coins, you
would fill out 3 total entries.
	n
	YSee Also:	n  HLQEDIT-QUEST-IN HLQEDIT-ASK HLQEDIT-ROOM
	n
#0
HLQEDIT-GIVE-COINS

	n
When you select the quest-in (quest entry) option of '	YGive Coins	n'
you will see this:
	n
How much coins?
	n
You would then enter the value of how many coins the mobile requires
on-hand to complete this quest-in (quest entry).  It is very important
to remember that this value counts how many coins the mobile has on-
hand, which means if the mobile is set to load with 100 coins and you
put a 100 coin value in this quest entry, then as soon as anybody
gives the quest-mobile even a single coin, it'll complete this quest-in
(quest entry).  So it is important to either set the mobiles coins at
0 or to make sure you add how many coints the mob loads with to the
value you require for your quest.  Upon filling this value you will be
returned to the 	RHLQEDIT-GIVE	n menu to optionally fill out more
quest-in (quest entries).  If you are done filling out your quest-in
info (quest entries), just select 0 and you will be brought to the
	RHLQEDIT-QUEST-OUT	n menu to continue the quest-building process.
	n
When you select the quest-in (quest entry) option of '	YGive Item	n'
you will see this:
	n
Select item(vnum)?
	n
You would at this point enter the vnum (	RVIRTUAL-NUMBERS	n) to select
which item the quest-mobile requires to fulfull this quest-in (quest
entry).  Upon filling this value you will be returned to the
	RHLQEDIT-GIVE	n menu to optionally fill out more quest-in (quest
entries).  If you are done filling out your quest-in info (quest 
entries), just select 0 and you will be brought to the
	RHLQEDIT-QUEST-OUT	n menu to continue the quest-building process.
	n
	YSee Also:	n  HLQEDIT-GIVE HLQEDIT-ASK HLQEDIT-ROOM
	n
#0
HLQEDIT-LOAD-OBJECT

	n
The load-object and load-mobile rewards will make an item
appear on the ground or a mobile appear in a given room.
When prompted for the room, you can select 0 to have the
quest-mobile load the mobile/object into the same room as
the quest-mobile.
	n
After entering this info, you will return to the quest-out
menu (	RHLQEDIT-QUEST-OUT	n) to add more rewards.
	n
	YSee Also:	n HLQEDIT-QUEST-OUT HLQEDIT
	n
