#0
HLQEDIT-QUEST-IN

The Homeland Quest System has two major elements in the system.

1)  Quest-In or Quest-Activator or Quest-Entry

2)  Quest-Out or Quest-Response/Reward

The Quest-In aspect of the system is the condition that will
start the quest and the menu looks like this:

What type of quest entry (G)ive, (R)oom or (A)sk?

(G)ive     	RHELP HLQEDIT-GIVE	n
(R)oom     	RHELP HLQEDIT-ROOM	n
(A)sk      	RHELP HLQEDIT-ASK	n

	YSee Also:	n  HLQEDIT-QUEST-OUT

#0
HLQEDIT-QUEST-OUT

	n
When you finish your quest-in (quest entries) for either
	RHLQEDIT-GIVE	n or 	RHLQEDIT-ROOM	n you will then be
brought to this menu, the quest-out (quest reward) menu:
	n
Quest-Out Menu (Quest Rewards)
C) Give coins                     	RHLQEDIT-COINS	n
I) Give item                      	RHLQEDIT-ITEM	n
O) Load object in a room          	RHLQEDIT-LOAD-OBJECT	n
M) Load mob in a room             	RHLQEDIT-LOAD-MOBILE	n
A) Attack questor                 	RHLQEDIT-ATTACK-QUESTOR	n
D) Disappear                      	RHLQEDIT-DISAPPEAR	n
T) Teach spell/skill (not yet implemented)
X) Open door in a room            	RHLQEDIT-OPEN-DOOR	n
F) Follow questor                 	RHLQEDIT-FOLLOW-QUESTOR	n
U) Set Church (not yet implemented)
K) Change Kit (not yet implemented)
S) Cast Spell                     	RHLQEDIT-CAST-SPELL	n
Enter choice (0 to end/quit):  
	n
After you select a reward, you will be brought back to
menu to select more rewards if you wish, if not just select
the '0' option to move to the 	RHLQEDIT-DIALOGUE	n menu to
finalize your quest.
	n
	YSee Also:	n HLQEDIT-DIALOGUE HLQEDIT
	n
#0
HLQEDIT-ROOM

	n
The '	Yroom quest	n' option for quest-in (quest entries) is a
quest that requires you to bring the quest-mobile to a particular
room with a given vnum (	RVIRTUAL-NUMBER	n).  In order for this
quest to be effective you will need to make sure the quest-mobile
is following the player, which can be accomplished via 	RTRIGEDIT	n
or through the 	RHLQEDIT-QUEST-OUT	n menu options.
	n
After you fill out the vnum, you will be brought to the next menu
	RHLQEDIT-QUEST-OUT	n to continue the quest building process.
	n
	YSee Also:	n  HLQEDIT-QUEST-OUT HLQEDIT
	n
