#0
HOLY-JAVELIN

	D>Usage:           	W cast 'holy javelin' (target)	n
	D>Accumulative:    	W  	n
	D>Duration:        	W 1 round + 1 round / 4 levels, maximum of 5 rounds 	n
	D>School of Magic: 	W Conjuration 	n
	D>Target(s):       	W Single Target 	n
	D>Magic Resist:    	W Yes 	n
	D>Saving Throw:    	W No 	n
	D>Damage Type:     	W Holy 	n
	D>Description:	n
	n
	nYou create a shimmering javelin of holy energy to hurl at an enemy as a ranged
	ntouched attack. The javelin deals 1d6 points of damage to an evil creature on a
	nsuccessful attack; it dissipates harmlessly against creatures of any other
	nalignment. Each round the target takes another 1d6 points of damage. For every 4
	ncaster levels you have, the javelin remains in the creature for an additional
	nround (to a maximum of 5 rounds at 18th level). While the creature remains
	nimpaled, it takes a –2 penalty on attack rolls and skill checks.

The holy
	njavelin glows like a torch, and this light clearly indicates the impaled
	ncreature’s location, cancelling any invisibility. Since this light is not a
	nlight effect, just the glow of a conjured javelin, darkness spells always
	nsuppress it, even if they are lower level.
	n
	n
	n
	YSee also:	n SPELLS
	n
