#0
HUNTING

   Hunting is a harvesting skill used to harvest animal hides.\n

#0
EXCHANGE HUNTS


Usage: hunts
       exchange (name of hunt trophy in inventory) (ring|bracer|pendant) <--- trinkets only
       list (trinkets | weapons)

The hunts system allows characters to seek out 'boss-style' mobs in the wilderness,
and kill them for hunting trophies and in some cases, enhanced crafting materials.

New hunts load every two hours, and are placed randomly in the wilderness map. At
any huntsmaster mob in the game (usually identified in their room description) you
can type 'hunts' to see what hunts are currently loaded.  A set of coordinates will
be specified where the hunt was last seen.  The hunt will be somewhere in the vicinity
of those coordinates. Often one will be required to travel between continents, through
magic, portals or by taking ships at the various seaports throughout the world.

Hunt mobs are usually too tough for a single character at the same level of the hunt
mob, so grouping up with other characters is recommended.  Defeating the hunt mob
will award nice exp, gold and quest points, as well as one or more hunt trophies
and potentially crafting materials in some cases.

These hunt trophies case be exchanged at a huntsmaster for a trinket (ring, pendant
or bracer) or a weapon oil (HELP WEAPON OILS), depending on the kind of hunt trophy.
You will need 10 of the same hunt trophy in order to exchange it.  You can type 'list'
at a huntsmaster to see what rewards are available.

See Also: WEAPON-ABILITIES, TRINKET-ABILITIES, WEAPON-OILS

--For exchanging in-game currency, see: CEXCHANGE

