#0
INQUISITOR-JUDGEMENTS

Inquisitors have the ability to perform a judgement on a foe they are fighting.

They are able to choose from among a number of different judgement affects.
Whenever they are in combat against the target they've judged, they receive
whatever benefits are associated with the judgement(s) they have active.

To see what judgements are available, type judgement list.

To toggle on or off a judgement effect, type judgement toggle (effect).

Initially, an inquisitor can only have one judgement effect active.  As they
gain inquisitor levels, they will be able to have more than one active at once.

When the inquisitor obtains the slayer feat, they will be able to use that command
to select one active judgement as their slayer effect.  This effect will be treated
as if the inquisitor were 5 levels higher when determining the bonus amount.
To assign a slayer effect, type: slayer (effect)

Finally, once the judgement effects are chosen, the inquisitor can perform the
judgement by typing: judgement enact. This judgement will last until the enemy dies,
or is judged by another player.

