IRON-GOLEM IRONGOLEM


Usage: wildshape iron golem
     : poisonbreath

An iron golem has a humanoid body made from iron. It can be sculpted into
any shape its creator desires, but it almost always displays armor of some
sort, from simple and utilitarian to ceremonial and ornate. Its features are
much smoother than those of a stone golem. Iron golems sometimes carry a
weapon in one hand, though they rarely use these, relying instead on their
slam attacks. An iron golem is 12 feet tall and weighs about 5,000 pounds. 

The Iron Golem is a wildshape option for members of the shifter prestige
class.  It offers damage reduction and complete spell immunity.  The exceptions
are fire magic, which heals the golem, and electrical magic, which will slow
the golem with no possibility of saving against it.  They are able to breathe
a cloud of poisonous gas once every 2 combat rounds.

