#0
JUNK

Usage: junk <object>
       junk <number> coins

Use JUNK instead of DROP if you want to keep the world a little cleaner.  If
you junk something, it will disappear and you'll get a few coins or experience
points, just as if you had dropped it in the dump.

Examples:

  > junk cup
  > junk all.bronze
  > junk 500 coins

See also: DONATE, DROP
#0
KAGONESTI-ELF RACE-KAGONESTI-ELF

\tG>Description:\tn
\n\tn
\n\tn
\n\tnAt home in the forests, the Kagonesti, or wild elves, believe
\n\tnevery creature and object, from insects and birds to rivers and clouds,
\n\tnpossesses a spirit. They honor these spirits and know that, in return, the
\n\tnspirits honor them. The Kagonesti believe that a happy life can only truly be
\n\tnachieved by harmoniously existing with nature. Passionate and proud, they want
\n\tnonly to be left to themselves. Due to the expansion of human nations and
\n\tnmistreatment by their own elven cousins, the Kagonesti have been dragged from
\n\tntheir forest homes and forced to live in a world they do not like or understand.
\n\tnUnlike their more placid kin, Kagonesti can be hottempered and fierce when
\n\tndriven to extremes. 
\n\tn
\n\tG>Racial Abilities:\tn
\n\tn
\n\tWInfravision:\tn            - Can detect life forms in the dark.
\n\tWMask of the Wild:\tn       - +3 to stealth checks.
\n\tWFleetness:\tn              - +20 stamina points per level.
\n\tWEnchantment Resistance:\tn - +2 to saves vs. enchantment.
\n\tWKeen Senses:\tn            - +2 to perception and sense motive skills.
\n\tWSleep immunity:\tn         - Immune to sleep based enchantments.
\n\tWElven Weapons:\tn          - Proficient in long swords, rapiers and all bow types.
\n\tn
\n\tG>Ability Adjustments:  \tW +2 Dex, +1 Str \tn
\n\tn
\n\tG>Experience Modifier:  \tW None \tn
\n\tn
\n\tYSee also:\tn RACES
\n\tn
\n
\n

#0
KAPAK-DRACONIAN RACE-KAPAK-DRACONIAN

\tG>Description:\tn
\n\tn
\n\tnKapak draconians are known for stealth, viciouscunning, and for
\n\tnlicking their blades with theirvenom-soaked tongues before battle. While
\n\tnnotknown for original thinking, kapaks exhibit cruelcreativity in carrying out
\n\tnassigned missions ofespionage and murder. Kapaks like structure in theirlives,
\n\tnand the military lifestyle suits them. Theirnatural talents for stealth and
\n\tnbutchery belie theirneed for order. Many become assassins, becausethey are adept
\n\tnat handling dangerous and constantlychanging situations. Female kapaks alsolike
\n\tnstructure, but they tend to be more nurturing,using their inborn healing
\n\tnabilities to aidother draconians. Kapaks are largerand more draconic than baaz,
\n\tnwith elongatedreptilian snouts, sharp-toothed maws, andhorned heads. They
\n\tnpossess two large glands intheir mouths that produce either poison (males)or a
\n\tnmagical healing saliva (females). They havescaly, green-tinged coppery hide, and
\n\tnsport apair of wings that extend 6 feet to each sidewhen outstretched. 
\n\tn
\n\tG>Racial Abilities:\tn
\n\tn
\n\tWUltravision:\tn                 - Can see in the dark.
\n\tWDraconian Bite:\tn              - Can make a bite attack as a swift action
\n\tWDraconian Kapak Scales:\tn      - Gets a +2 Natural Armor Class bonus
\n\tWDraconian Disease Immunity:\tn  - Immune to disease
\n\tWDraconian Gallop:\tn            - Gains extra movement points when levelling
\n\tWDraconian Devotion:\tn          - Gains combat bonuses when grouped with dragons or other draconians
\n\tWDraconian Controlled Fall:\tn   - Fall damage is reduced
\n\tWBozak Death Throes:\tn          - When a bozak is killed, bones explode dealing AoE piercing damage
\n\tWDraconian Spell Resistance :\tn - Gains 10 + level spell resistance
\n\tWSneak Attack:\tn                - Gains 1 rank of sneak attack
\n\tWApply Poison:\tn                - Proficient in applying poisons to weapons
\n\tWKapak Saliva :\tn               - Males can lick their weapons to poison them, females can lick others to heal them.\t
\n\tn
\n\tG>Ability Adjustments:  \tW +2 Con, +4 Dex \tn
\n\tn
\n\tG>Experience Modifier:  \tW 1.5x \tn
\n\tn
\n\tYSee also:\tn RACES
\n\tn

#0
KEEN-EDGE

	D>Usage:           	W cast 'keen edge' (target)	n
	D>Accumulative:    	W  	n
	D>Duration:        	W 10 minutes / level 	n
	D>School of Magic: 	W Transmutation 	n
	D>Target(s):       	W Single Target 	n
	D>Magic Resist:    	W N/A 	n
	D>Saving Throw:    	W N/A 	n
	D>Damage Type:     	W N/A 	n
	D>Description:	n
	n
	nThis spell makes a weapon magically keen, improving its ability to deal telling
	nblows. This transmutation doubles the threat range of the weapon. A threat range
	nof 20 becomes 19-20, a threat range of 19-20 becomes 17-20, and a threat range
	nof 18-20 becomes 15-20. The spell can only take effect on piercing or slashing
	nweapons.

Multiple effects that increase a weapon’s threat range (such as
	nthe keen special weapon property and the Improved Critical feat) don’t stack.
	n
	n
	n
	YSee also:	n SPELLS
	n
#0
KENDER RACE-KENDER

\tG>Description:\tn
\n\tn
\n\tnTo the other races, kender are the child-race of Krynn. The diminutive kender
\n\tnhave short attention spans, intense curiosity, and a fearlessness that serves
\n\tnthem well in battle, but often lands them (and those traveling with them) in
\n\tndanger. Kender live a carefree existence where every new day is a day of
\n\tnwonderful secrets just waiting to be discovered. Their most defining character
\n\tntraits are their insatiable curiosity and their utter fearlessness, which makes
\n\tnfor a frightening combination. All dark caves need exploring, all locked doors
\n\tnneed opening, and all chests hide something interesting. Young kender around
\n\tnthe age of 20 or so are afflicted with wanderlust, an intense desire to
\n\tndepart their homeland and set out on a journey of discovery.
\n\tnPhysical boundaries or notions of privacy are both alien concepts to them,
\n\tnwhile the monetary value of an object means nothing to them. They are as likely
\n\tnto be more captivated by the feather of goat-sucker bird as by a sapphire.
\n\tnKender are never happier than when their hands are in the pockets, pouches, or
\n\tnbackpacks of those around them. Kender do not consider such appropriation to be
\n\tnthievery as others understand it (kender are as contemptuous of thieves as the
\n\tnnext person). Kender term this handling or borrowing because they firmly
\n\tnintend to return what they pilfer to the proper owner.
\n\tn
\n\tG>Racial Abilities:\tn
\n\tn
\n\tWInfravision:\tn            - Can detect life forms in the dark.
\n\tWHoopak Proficiency:\tn     - Can wield hoopaks
\n\tWSkill Modifiers:\tn        - +2 bonus to stealth, bluff, perception, disable device 
\n\tn                          and sleight of hand skills. They receive a -4 penalty 
\n\tn                          to concentration.
\n\tWBorrowing:\tn              - Kender have access to the 'borrow' command and ability.
\n\tWKender Taunt:\tn           - +4 bonus when using the taunt ability. Taunts only use 
\n\tn                          a swift action.
\n\tWKender Fearlessness:\tn    - Kender are immune to all forms of fear.
\n\tn
\n\tG>Ability Adjustments:  \tW +2 Dex, -2 Wis, -2 Str \tn
\n\tn
\n\tG>Experience Modifier:  \tW None \tn
\n\tn
\n\tYSee also:\tn RACES
\n\tn
\n
\n

#0
KEYCHECK

   Keycheck <zone vnum> OR Keycheck with no argument OR keycheck .  Will check
the zone you are standing in .  This command will check all the rooms & objects
in the given zone for keys that do not match the zone's object range.

#0
KEYS

Usage: unlock [door]

If you find a locked door use a key to open it. You must have the correct key 
in your inventory to unlock a door.

See also: OPEN

