#0
LEVEL-DRAIN

   Some enemies, particularly some kinds of powerful undead, are able to inflict
level drain upon their victims.  Each point of level drain reduces your ability
score modifiers, skill checks, combat maneuver and defense checks, saving throws
and attack rolls by 1.
#0
LEVEL LEVELING LEVELLING

	jWhat are 	JLevels of Experience?	n
	b-------------------------------------------------------------------------------	n
Character levels are the abstract, basic comparison of relative player power in
Luminari.  When you gain enough experience, you gain a level, which depending
on the level gained, allows you additional skill points, additional attribute
points, and additional feats.  Your title also changes as you level, the
specifics of which vary depending on class.
 
	JGaining Levels of Experience	j in Luminari	n
	b-------------------------------------------------------------------------------	n
When you have enough experience to advance to another level in experience, the
game will prompt you that you can do so.  You can then use GAIN <class> to gain
a level of experience in this class.  You can choose any such class you desire,
however, you can only possess up to three different classes.
 
It should be noted, that you cannot GAIN another level in any class, until you
have advanced your current level fully, by using attribute BOOSTs you have
available, gaining FEATs, and TRAINing your skills.
 
	jHow to 	Jboost attributes	n
	b-------------------------------------------------------------------------------	n
	pMain article: 	oHELP BOOST, HELP STATISTICS	n
 
As you gain in experience, you will slowly be able to hone and improve your
physical and mental attributes.  Every four levels, you gain the ability to
BOOST one of your attributes, increasing it and in turn increasing the bonuses
you get from it.
 
To BOOST an attribute, just type 	YBOOST <attribute>	n, for example, 	YBOOST STRENGTH	n.
If you want to know your current attributes, you can view them in 	YSCORE	n.
 
	jHow to 	Jgain a feat	n
	b-------------------------------------------------------------------------------	n
	pMain article: 	oHELP FEAT-SYSTEM, HELP STUDY	n
 
There are many special feats you can gain as you level - every three non-epic
levels in a class, you gain an additional feat from a pool of feats available
that chosen class.  Some classes gain additional bonus feats.  Feats grant you
additional special powers or abilities, such as the ability to dual wield
weapons, power attack, and so forth.
 
To gain a feat, you need to find a TRAINER, and then 	YSTUDY	n.  STUDY allows you
access to a variety of character specials.  From there, you can select 1 for
feats, and then you are presented with the different categories of feats.
Select the category that you are interested in by entering its number and
pressing enter, and once over again for the feat that interests you, then, if
you quit all the way out of these menus, and select YES to save, you will now
possess the additional feat.
 
	jHow to 	Jtrain a skill	n
	b-------------------------------------------------------------------------------	n
	pMain article: 	oHELP SKILLS, HELP TRAIN	n
 
With every level you gain, so do you hone your skills.  You will gain sessions
you can use to train those skills at a trainer, to grow those skills and your
abilities within them.
 
If you use 	YTRAIN	n just by itself, you will gain a list of what skills are
available to you, how much you have trained in the skills currently, what the
bonus from that skill is as a result of your skill points and the attribute(s)
that affect that skill, as well as whether they are cross-class or class skills.
 
A class skill is one your class is proficient in naturally, and as such, comes
naturally to you.  As a result, you can learn it normally.  In contrast, a
cross-class skill is a skill you can still learn, but isn't natural to the
class.  These skills take two training sessions to train, and you can only
train them if you have enough points.
 
When you have decided what skill(s) you want to train, you just need to find a
trainer, and then use 	YTRAIN <skill>	n.
	b-------------------------------------------------------------------------------	n
	pSee also: 	oSKILLS, ATTRIBUTES, BOOST, TRAIN, FEAT-SYSTEM, LEVELS, STUDY	n
#0
LEVELS


Usage: levels [<min>-<max> | <range>]

Displays exp required for levels.
levels       - shows all levels (1-30)
levels 5     - shows 5 levels either side of your current level
levels 10-30 - shows level 10 to level 30

See also: experience

#0
LEVITATE LEVITATE-SPELL SPELL-LEVITATE

Levitate

Levitation will keep the target hovering above the ground.  This
will allow you to cross shallow water without a boat, it will save
you from falling into pits or even break your fall if you are able to
cast it before hitting the ground.

