#0
ABJURE CHANT COMPEL COMPOSE CONCOCT MEDITATE MEMORIZATION MEMORIZE PRAY PRAYER

usage:  memorize <wizard spell name>
usage:  prayer <cleric prayer name>
usage:  commune <druid spell name>
usage:  meditate
usage:  adjure <ranger spell name>
usage:  compose
usage:  chant <paladin spell name>
usage:  concoct <alchemist extract>
usage:  compel
also:  memorize / prayer / commune / chant / adjure / concoct <without any argument>

Preparing spells is a two-step process.  First you select which spells you
want to have available, then you actually prepare them.  After casting, 
you simply have to re-prepare - you don't need to select spells again unless
you want to change them.

Step 1:
Wizards, druids, clerics, rangers, alchemists and paladins all prepare a list of the spells
they want to have available.  This is accomplished by typing "memorize '<spell name>'",
"commune '<spell name>'", etc.  If you want to cast a spell more than once per rest, 
you need to prepare it multiple times.
Sorcerers and bards simply choose which spells they have available in the "study" menu.

Step 2:
When you are ready to prepare spells, first you must "rest", and then "memorize", "commune", 
etc.  ** YOU MUST BE RESTING TO PREPARE! **
Once you do, you will begin readying the spells in your queue (or recovering spell slots).

See also:  SPELLS FORGET

See:  SPELL-PRAYER for spell info

#0
MEMTIME-DISPLAY

This toggle will show your remaining memorization time
for the next spell in your memorization list.  This can
be modified via PREFEDIT menu.

See Also:  PREFEDIT

