#0
MERCIES PALADIN-MERCIES


Paladins begin to gain mercies at level 3 and every 3rd level thereafter.
Mercies are additional effects that take place when using the paladin's
lay on hands ability. Most of them remove a specific kind of debuff, though
there are others that offer a beneficial effect for a time. Not all mercies
are available right away.  As you gain paladin levels, more mercies will open
up to you for selection.  Mercies can be chosen in the study menu.

Paladin Mercies Available
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Deceived        : removes effects from taunt or intimidate
Fatigued        : removes fatigue from rage or other sources
Shaken          : removes shaken status
Dazed           : removes dazed status
Enfeebled       : removes effects that reduce strength or constitution
Staggered       : removes staggered status
Confused        : removes confused status
Cursed          : removes curses on a person (not items though)
Frightened      : removes fear status
Injured         : gives regeneration of 3 hp/round for duration of 1/2 paladin levels
Nauseated       : removes nauseated status
Poisoned        : removes poison status
Blinded         : removes blindess
Deafened        : removes deafness
Ensorcelled     : removes 1 random negative effect
Paralyzed       : removes paralysis
Stunned         : removes stunned status

See Also: LAYONHANDS, PALADIN
#0
METALWORKING

   Metalworking is a crafting skill used to make misc.  Metal items.\n

#0
MAXIMIZED METAMAGIC QUICKENED

	n
Spellcasters, both Arcane and Divine, can now twist the arcanic fields to their will through the use of Metamagic!
	n
Prepared spellcasters must prepare their spells slightly differently now, no matter if they cast mundane magicks or those altered by metamagic.  The names of the spell they are preparing must now be enclosed in quotes ().  Metamagical alterations to the spell come before the spells name, as seen in the following example:
	n
mem quickened maximized 'magic missile'
	n
This will memorize a quickened, maximized magic missile spell (as a Wizard).  The metamagic feats have the following modifiers associated with them:
A quickened spell will have its circle increased by 4
A maximized spell will have its circle increased by 3
	n
Casting a spell affected by metamagic is similar:
	n
cast quickened maximized 'magic missile' target
	n
This, along with the preparation command, can be shortened thus:
	n
cast q m 'magic missile' target
	n
It should be noted you can also shorten the cast command and spell name resulting in:
	n
c q m 'm m' target
	n
Only the feats Quicken Spell and Maximize Spell have been implemented so far.  Please give feedback and report any bugs you find with the system!
	n
