#0
MINOTAUR RACE-MINOTAUR

\tG>Description:\tn
\n\tn
\n\tn
\n\tnAt home both on land and at sea, minotaurs live in an honor-based
\n\tnsociety where strength determines power in both the gladiatorial arenas and in
\n\tndaily life. Minotaurs believe in the superiority of their race above all others.
\n\tnThey believe their destiny is to rule the world. From youth, minotaurs are
\n\tntrained in combat and warfare and instilled with a strict code of honor. The
\n\tnmilitaristic society of minotaurs gives them a rigid view of the world, clearly
\n\tndelineated in black and white. Minotaurs value strength, cunning, and
\n\tnintelligence. The ultimate test of all three virtues is conducted in the Great
\n\tnCircus, an annual contest held in a gladiatorial arena. 
\n\tn
\n\tG>Racial Abilities:\tn
\n\tn
\n\tWSeafaring:\tn          - +2 to swim checks.
\n\tWMinotaur Toughness:\tn - +2 to intimidation checks.
\n\tWTough Hide:\tn         - +1 to armor class (natural ac bonus).
\n\tWInfravision:\tn        - limited vision when without light.
\n\tn
\n\tG>Ability Adjustments:  \tW +4 Str, -2 Int and -2 Dex  \tn
\n\tn
\n\tG>Experience Modifier:  \tW None \tn
\n\tn
\n\tYSee also:\tn RACES
\n\tn
\n

