Usage: moves
#0
MOVE-ACTION


A move action allows you to take a physical action, most commonly to stand 
from a prone position or to flee from combat.  Regular movement requires 
that you have a move action available, but generally does not consume a move
action.  
 
Some additional examples of move actions include:
 
- Quaffing a potion (using the 	Yquaff	n command)
- Opening or closing a door (using the 	Yopen	n or 	Yclose	n command)
- Disengaging from combat (using the 	Ydisengage	n command)
 
You can take a move action in place of a standard action.
 
	YSee Also:	n Combat, Standard-action, Swift-action
#0
MSGEDIT

Usage:  msgedit
To view the list of damage messages

Usage:  msgedit <#> (The # is the far left value shown when you type 'msgedit')

The 'msgedit' command is the command for editing damage messages for skills
and spells in-game.  It is very self explanatory, and you can have multiple
sets of messages for each attack-type/spell/skill for variety.  Color can
(and should) be added (to help players distinguish normal activity from
damaging attacks/spells/skills).

On the list via the 'msgedit' command without any argument, you will notice
entries labeled as "Unknown" or "UNUSED" in the list.  You will have to view
those entries to see which entry they correspond to.

See Also:  OLC
#0
MUD

"Dirt + Water" -Fizban 2018
#0
MULTICLASS

Multi-classing is the ability to select how you advance your training.

There are different systems of "multi-classing."  The system we are NOT
using is advancing completely in one class, then adding another class
on top of it.

Our system of multi-classing means that you are sacrificing advancement
in one class in the preference of the diversity offered by advancing in
another class.

Example:  You started as a 1st level Warrior and have gained enough
experience to advance to the 2nd level.  You can choose to continue your
advancement as a Warrior, thus increasing your melee-combat prowess or
if you QUALIFY for a different class, you can advance in that class...
let's say Wizard.

If you had selected to advance a level as a Wizard, you now would be
2nd level character, with one level as a Warrior and one level as a
Wizard.  That means you wouldn't have gained the melee-combat advance-
ment you would have gained as a Warrior, BUT you will gain some magic
casting abilities as a Wizard.

Some special notes is to bear in mind that some classes will enhance each
other better, in addition you have to QUALIFY to advance in the desired
class, finally there is a MAXIMUM-MULTICLASS value that is set by the
game that limits the number of classes you can take on.

See also:  MAXIMUM-MULTICLASS QUALIFY GAIN
