NEWBIE

Welcome to LuminariMUD!  Here are some helpful commands to get you
started:

HELP
HELP TELEPORTER
COMMANDS
HINDEX <help keyword>

See Also:  HELP TELEPORTER COMMANDS HINDEX
#0
NEWCRAFT

craft itemtype     : set whether the item is weapon, armor, jewelry, instrument or misc.
\ncraft specifictype : set what kind of the type will be made. Eg. for a weapon, could be long sword.
\ncraft keywords     : sets the keywords of the object.
\ncraft shortdesc    : sets the short description of the object, seen as the name of the item.
\ncraft roomdesc     : sets what is displayed when the item is on the floor of a room.
\ncraft extradesc    : sets what is displayed if someone looks at the item.
\ncraft bonuses      : set the bonuses on the item (more info below).
\ncraft display      : show the status of your current crafting project.
\ncraft reset        : resets the crafting project to default values. Essentially deletes the craft.
\n
\nFor bonuses, an object can have up to six of them. The command syntax is as follows:
\ncraft bonuses (slot) (location) (bonus type) (modifier) (specifier)
\n
\nThe breakdown of the syntax is as follows:
\nslot: which slot number to add the bonus. From 1-6.
\nlocation: what will te bonus affect? Ie. strength, reflex, hit points.
\nbonus type: for crafted items this is restricted to either enhancement or universal. Armor class will also
\n-- allow deflection and natural. Since the universal type stacks, the modifier will be divided by three if set
\n-- to universal bonus type.
\nmodifier: this is how much the bonus will be for the stat applied.
\nspecifier: only used for certain bonus locations: feats, skills and spell slots.
\n-- feats: you would specify the feat name using dashes instead of spaces.
\n-- Eg. craft bonus 0 feat enhancement 1 improved-initiative
\n-- This would give the person the improved initiative feat when wearing the item.
\n-- Note that the modifier on feat bonuses can never be more than one.
\n-- skills: you would specify the skill name
\n-- Eg. craft bonus 0 skill enhancement 1 sleight-of-hand
\n-- this would increase the person's sleight of hand skill by 1
\n-- spell slots: you would specify the class name
\n-- Eg. craft bonus 0 spell-circle-3 enhancement 1 paladin
\n-- would add 1 3rd level spell slot for a character's paladin spell list

