	nis, in the heart of the paladin, a personal test - an opportunity
	nto demonstrate bravery, to learn tactics and to find ways to do good.
	nDivine power protects these warriors of virtue, warding off harm,
	nprotecting from disease, healing and guarding against fear.  The
	npaladin can also direct this power to help others, healing wounds or
	ncuring diseases and also use it to destroy evil.  Experienced
	npaladins can smite evil foes and turn away undead.  A paladin's
	nWisdom score helps determine maximum spell level and many of the
	npaladin's special abilities are affected by Charisma.
