#0
PERFORM

Bardic Performance

To start a performance: perform <name of performance>
To stop a performance: perform
To replace the primary performance: perform replace <name>
To add a second performance with Master of Motifs: perform add <name>
To stop one performance: perform stop <name>

When not performing, typing 'perform' will list your available performances.

The perform command is the entry point for bardic performances.  Each performance
varies by type (example: song vs dance), ideal instrument (example: lyre vs drum),
and target of performance effect (example: offensive vs defensive).  An instrument
is optional, but performing without one or with the wrong type reduces effectiveness.

The first verse occurs immediately.  Later verses repeat approximately every 11 seconds
until you stop, stutter, become unable to perform, disconnect, or interrupt the performance.
Persistent effects normally last two combat rounds, long enough to overlap the next verse.
Audible performances do not affect recipients who are deaf.  Dance and act performances
are visual and do not require the recipient to hear them.

Knowing the performance feat determines whether you can perform it.  Your trained Perform
ability and the quality and suitability of an instrument improve effectiveness and reduce
the chance of a stutter; they are not additional start requirements.

	RSee also:	Y performance-difficulty performance-effectiveness performance-verse
     performance-stutter	n

