#0
PERFORMANCE-DIFFICULTY PERFORMANCE-EFFECTIVENESS PERFORMANCE-STUTTER PERFORMANCE-VERSE

	n 
	n PERFORMANCE STUTTER
	n
	n Stuttering your performance means failing a difficulty check to complete your
	n performance.  This check can be augmented by using the correct instrument of high
	n quality.
	n 
	n PERFORMANCE VERSE
	n 
	n Assuming you do not stutter your performance, your performance will automatically
	n continue indefinitely.  The first verse occurs immediately and later verses repeat
	n approximately every 11 seconds.  Persistent effects normally last 2 combat rounds;
	n Lingering Performance adds 3 more rounds.  Songweaver adds 1 round and 1 point of
	n effectiveness per combined rank.
	n 
	n PERFORMANCE EFFECTIVENESS
	n 
	n Performing without any sort of performance instrument will give the highest penalty.
	n Using any instrument with your performance will reduce that penalty, and using the proper
	n instrument will remove all penalties.  In addition some magical instruments will further
	n enhance the effectiveness of your performance.  Engaging in combat while performing will
	n give a significant reduction in performance effectiveness.  Your trained ability perform
	n can give you a bonus to effectiveness.
	n 
	n PERFORMANCE DIFFICULTY
	n 
	n Performance difficulty can be offset by instruments.  If the song is difficult, you might
	n stutter and have to restart the performance.
	n 
	n 	RSee also:	Y perform	n
	n
#0
PET-SHOPS

	n
There are three methods for creating pet shops.  You can use DGScripts,
"pet" item type spec proc, or "pet store" room spec proc.  The procedure
for each follows.
	n
DGScript Pet Shop
We set up a sample pet shop, please 	RTSTAT 338	n for an example of a pet
shop that is scripted.
	n
Pet Item Type and Object Spec Proc
You create an object and mobile with matching vnumbers, make sure the
object is of item type "Pet."  Then ask a coder to set your object
spec proc as "bought_pet."  It will not work until the code is changed
and the MUD is rebooted.
Then you just place that object in a shop like any other purchased good.
	n
Room Spec Proc
Make two rooms and some pets. The rooms MUST be sequential. if the
first room is 315 then the second must be 316. The second room is known as the 
storeroom. All that is required in the storeroom is to load one of each mob you
wish to be a pet. This room can not have any exits and will never be used by 
mortals. Although a pet shopkeeper is not required it is recommended. After 
all of this is done ask your coder to implement the petshop. It will not work 
until the code is changed and the MUD is rebooted. The cost of pets is 300 
times their level.
	n
See also: SHOPS, SPECIALS
	n
