#0
PIXIE PIXIE-DUST PIXIE-INVISIBILITY PIXIEDUST PIXIEINVISIBILITY

Usage: wildshape pixie
     : pixieinvis
     : pixiedust (target) (sleep|charm|confuse|dispel|entangle|shield)

Perhaps the best-known and most elusive of all fey creatures, pixies live 
in the deepest, most pristine forests, but their insatiable curiosity often
leads them far from home. Most pixies stand just over 2 feet tall, though
they typically fly about the eye level of creatures they are conversing
with in order to maintain eye contact. Their weight is around 30 pounds. Pixies
talk quickly and easily become overexcited.

The Pixie is a wildshape option available to members of the shifter
prestige class.  They are able to fly, have the dodge, weapon finesse and
infravision feats and can use the pixie dust and pixie invisibility commands.

Pixie dust allows the pixie to cause a specified affect to take place on the
chosen target.  Options are sleep, charm, confusion, entangle, dispel magic
and a magical shield. They can use the pixie dust command up to
4 + their natural charisma score, times per day.

Pixie invisibility allows the pixie to cast greater invisibility at will with
the pixieinvis command.

They also have 10 damage reduction and 15 spell resistance.

#0
PKILL PKRULES PLAYER-KILL PLAYERKILL

PKILL

PKILL or player-killing is the act of attacking another player.  As of the
writing of this file, player-killing is fully enabled for the purpose of
testing.  Our rule for player-killing in general right now is that it is
only allowed with consent.  I.E. you must challenge the victim and they
must consent before attacking or stealing from them.  These rules will
likely change in the future to either support a fully open player-killing
environment or possibly to completely disable player-killing.

If there is any doubt, please refer to our POLICY file and/or ask
Staff.

