#0
PSIONIC-AUGMENTING


Many psionic powers can be made more powerful through the process of augmenting.
This process involves using extra psp when manifesting a power using the 
manifest command. A power's help file will usually indicate whether the power 
can be augmented, and what form the augmentation takes mechanically.

However, there are certain rules that come into play when augmenting:

1. You need to have enough psp to cover the cost of the power and any augment
   psp you're going to add.

2. You cannot use more augment psp than your augment limit.  By default, your
   augment limit is your psionicist class level minus the base psp cost of the
   power. For example, if your psionicist class level is 10, and you want to
   manifest the biofeedback power, with a base psp cost of 3, then your augment
   psp limit is 7.  Some feats and other affects can increase this limit.

3. Many powers use augment points in certain increments, and some others have
   caps on how many you can use. For example, in the biofeedback power manifestation
   above, the DR bonus on biofeedback only increases by one per 3 augment psp
   spent. Some other powers might not let you spend more than a certain number
   of augment psp.

4. Using augment psp on a power may increase the manfesting time of a power.
   In this calculation, the first two augment psp you use will not increase a
   power's manifestation time. Every 2 augment psp used beyond those first two
   free ones will increase the casting time by 1 second. A power's manifestation
   time can not be reduced below 1 second.  Some feats and affects may also reduce
   this increased manifestation time.
