#0
QUIT

When you get tired of playing, you can leave the game by typing 'quit'.
You can quit anywhere, and you will not lose your EQ when you decide to do so.

See also: INN, OFFER, RENT
#0
QUIVERING-PALM QUIVERINGPALM

This ability will allow the Monk to strike a vital area of their opponent.
Potentially slaying them instantly.  The monk will receive bonus damage to
their next attack after quivering palm is triggered.  If their opponent
is lower level than themselves they will be forced to make a fortitude save
or die instantly from the attack.

Usage: quiveringpalm
#0
RACE RACES

	n
RACE RACES
	n
Usage: race <list|info|feats> <race name>
	n
There is a wide variety of playable races on LuminariMUD.  The
race command is a convenient way to quickly look up info about
various races.
	n
There are 3 category of playable races: normal, advanced and epic.
The normal races are accessible for character creation to all
players.  The advanced and epic races are unlockable via the accexp
system.
	n
See Also:  ACCEXP ACCOUNT LOCKED-RACES EPIC-RACES
	n
#0
AASIMAR AASIMIR ASIMAR ASIMIR RACE-AASIMAR RACE-AASIMIR RACE-ASIMAR RACE-ASIMIR

	G>Description:	n
	n
	n
Aasimar were human-based planetouched, native outsiders that had
in their blood some good, otherworldly characteristics. They were often, but not
always, descended from celestials and other creatures of pure good alignment,
but while predisposed to good alignments, aasimar were by no means always good.
Aasimar bore the mark of their celestial touch through many different physical
features that often varied from individual to individual. Most commonly, aasimar
were very similar to humans, like tieflings and other planetouched. Nearly all
aasimar were uncommonly beautiful and still, and they were often significantly
taller than humans as well. 
	n
	G>Racial Abilities:	n
	n
	WUltravision:	n          - Can see in the dark.
	WHealing Hands:	n        - Can cast regeneration 3 times/day.
	WLight Bearer:	n         - Can cast daylight 3 times/day.
	WCelestial Resistance:	n - Receives 5/- damage reduction against cold, acid and electric damage.
	WAstral Majesty:	n       - Receives +1 dodge bonus to ac and +1 to all saves when combat target's
	n               	n         hit points are less than 50 percent of their maximum hit points.
	n
	G>Ability Adjustments:  	W +2 Cha, +1 Wis  	n
	n
	G>Experience Modifier:  	W None 	n
	n
	YSee also:	n RACES
	n
#0
DRAGON-BORN DRAGONBORN RACE-DRAGON-BORN RACE-DRAGONBORN

	G>Description:	n
	n
	n
Dragonborn (also known as Strixiki in Draconic; or Vayemniri,
"Ash-Marked Ones", in Tymantheran draconic) were a race of draconic creatures
native to Abeir, Toril's long-sundered twin. During the Spellplague, dragonborn
were transplanted from Abeir to Toril, the majority of them living in the
continent of Laerakond in the 15th century DR. In Faerun, most dragonborn dwelt
in the militaristic nation of Tymanther. 
	n
	G>Racial Abilities:	n
	n
	WDragonborn Resistance:	n    - Gain 5/- damage reduction against the element associated with their dragon ancestry.
	WDragonborn Breath Weapon:	n - Deals area of effect elemental damage of the type associated with their dragon ancestry.
	WDragonborn Fury:	n          - Gain +1 to attack rolls and +2 to damage if below 50% max hit points.
