#0
CLASS-ROGUE ROGUE

	m-----------------------------------------------------------------	n
	m>Description:	n
	n
Rogues have little in common with each other.  While some - maybe
even the majority - are stealthy rogues, many serve as scouts, spies,
investigators, diplomats or simple thugs.  Rogues are versatile,
adaptable and skilled at getting what others don't want them to get.
While not equal to fighters in combat, a rogue knows how to hit where
it hurts, and a backstab can dish out a lot of damage.  Rogues also
seem to have a sixth sense when it comes to avoiding danger.
Experienced rogues develop nearly magical power and skills as they
master the arts of stealth, evasion and backstab.  In addition, while
not capable of casting spells, a rogue can sometimes 'fake it' well
enough to cast spells from scrolls, activate wands and use various
other magical items.
	n
	m>Class Abilities:	n
	n
	Ytype: 	Rclass rogue	n to view the complete list of class feats.
	n
	m>Alignment:     	W Any 	n
	m>Hit Dice:      	W 3-6 Per Level 	n
	m>Skill Points:  	W Int Modifier x 4 at 1st level, 8 + Int Modifier
each additional level	n
	m>Proficiencies:	n
	WAdvanced Weapon Proficiency	n
	WLight Armor Proficiency	n
	n
	YSee also:	n CLASSES BACKSTAB
	n
