#0
SINGLEFILE

Singlfile rooms are tunnel-like rooms that are not big enough
to allow more than one person at a time pass through unless
in a 'reclining' position.

Staff can use the 'singlefile' command to list all the rooms
that are singlefile in the game.

See Also:  RECLINING

#0
SIZE-CLASS SIZES

Size classes apply to characters/mobiles/objects, they are as follow:
  Fine
Diminutive
Tiny
Small
Medium
Large
Huge
Gargantuan
Colossal

Mobiles that are smaller than you tend to be harder to hit.  But you will be able
to use larger weapons than the smaller mobile.

See also:  MOB-SIZE TWO-HANDED-WEAPON
#0
SIZE-DIFFERENCE

In some scenarios, such as attempts at hitting and attempts at spotting,
the size of the attempter versus the size of the victim is relevant.

A character that is smaller than you will be harder to hit and spot,
but will suffer more damage if you do land a blow due to your bigger
size.

The default calculation for this bonus/penalty is:
Size-Class Difference Between the Two parties * 2

See Also:  HIDE
