SMITE-EVIL SMITEEVIL

This ability will allow the user to channel the powers of Good
to strike down the Evil foe before them.  The user will gain
bonus damage to their attack based on their Charisma.

If the target is not of Evil alignment this ability will have no
affect.

Usage: smiteevil
#0
SMITE-GOOD SMITEGOOD

This ability will allow the user to channel the powers of Evil
to strike down the Good foe before them.  The user will gain
bonus damage to their attack based on their Charisma.
If the target is not of Good alignmemt this ability will have no
affect.

Usage: smitegood
#0
MOVE-SILENTLY SNEAK


Usage: sneak

Using sneak will attempt to move quietly between rooms while in the
"sneak" mode.  A perception check by those in the rooms will determine
if you are successful or not.

Your skill in stealth will determine success.

	YSee Also	n:  PERCEPTION HIDE STEALTH


#0
SNEAK-ATTACK


Some classes are able to catch an opponent off guard, when he/she is unable to
properly defend him/herself from attacks, resulting in an attack that will
strike vital spots for extra damage.

The elements that will help you accomplish a sneak attack:

Opponent is flat-footed (FF)
Opponent somehow lost his/her dexterity bonus (Dx)
Opponent is flanked (Fk)

#0
SOCIALS

Usage: socials

The SOCIALS command generates a canonical listing of all available socials.

Usage: <social> [target] <body part>

Socials are commands used to show your affective state to others.  The
actor, victim and bystanders may receive different messages.  Generally,
social commands are used only to express emotion and not to take action,
but it is possible that some mobs (or players) will take action based on
the social.  (Slap a dragon lately?)

Examples:

  > shake homer
  > applaud marge
  > kiss rumble foot

See also: EMOTE, GEMOTE
#0
CLASS-SORCERER SORCERER

	m-----------------------------------------------------------------	n
	m>Description:	n
	n
	nSorcerers are arcane spellcasters who manipulate magic energy with
	nimagination and talent rather than studious discipline.  They have
	nno books, no mentors, no theories - just raw power that they direct
	nat will.  Sorcerers know fewer spells than wizards, and acquire
	nthem more slowly, but they can cast individual spells more often
	nand have no need to prepare their incantations ahead of time.  Also
	nunlike wizards, sorcerers cannot specialize in a school of
	nmagic.  Since sorcerers gain their powers without undergoing the
	nyears of rigourous study that wizards go through, they have a
	nbit more time to learn fighting skills.  Charisma is very important
	nfor sorcerers - the higher the value, the higher spell level she
	ncan cast.
