AQUEOUS-ORB SPELL-AQUEOUS-ORB

	D>Usage:           	W cast 'aqueous orb' (target)	n
	D>Accumulative:    	W  	n
	D>Duration:        	W 1 round / level 	n
	D>School of Magic: 	W Conjuration 	n
	D>Target(s):       	W Single Target 	n
	D>Magic Resist:    	W Yes 	n
	D>Saving Throw:    	W Reflex (See Below) 	n
	D>Damage Type:     	W Water 	n
	D>Description:	n
	n
	nThis spell conjures forth a large ball of rolling water that advances on its
	ntarget, engulfing them within. Creatures who are engulfed will take 2d6 water
	ndamage per round unless they succeed at a reflex save.  On a successful save the
	nspell does no damage that round, except for creatures of a fire subtype, who
	ntake 2d6 damage on a successful reflex save and 4d6 on a failed one.

	nThe spell will cancel any fire effects the creature is under, such as fire shield,
	ncontinual flame and others. The spell will not do any damage to creatures who
	ncan breathe water or do not need to breathe. It will also not do damage to
	ncreatures who are of size huge or larger.

	nThis spell will also remove any walls of fire in the room.
	n
	nNote that the damaging aspect of this spell will only proc if the caster is in combat,
	nand will automatically target the person the caster is fighting.
	n
	YSee also:	n SPELLS
	n
#0
BANISHING-BLADE SPELL-BANISHING-BLADE

	D>Usage:           	W cast 'banishing blade'	n
	D>Accumulative:    	W  	n
	D>Duration:        	W 1 round / level 	n
	D>School of Magic: 	W Abjuration 	n
	D>Target(s):       	W Self Only 	n
	D>Magic Resist:    	W Yes 	n
	D>Saving Throw:    	W Will (special) 	n
	D>Damage Type:     	W  	n
	D>Description:	n
	n
	nThis spell will conjure forth a green longsword of pure energy.  The blade does
	nnot attack in a traditional sense.  Instead, it will attempt to trip any who
	nmake a successful melee attack against you, once per round. If the trip is
	nsuccessful, the creature will be immune to the banishing blade effects for 4
	nrounds. If the trip is successful and the attacker is a mob that has been
	nbrought forth from various summoning spells, it must make a willpower save or be
	nbanished and dismissed from the mob's owner.  A successful will save will still
	nstagger the mob for 1 round, and the mob will not be vulnerable to banishment
	nfor another 4 rounds. Note that the banishing affects will not work at all on
	nmobs of a greater level than that of the banishing blade wielder.
	n
	n
	n
	YSee also:	n SPELLS
	n
#0
BLACK-TENTACLES SPELL-BLACK-TENTACLES

	D>Usage:           	W cast 'black tentacles' (target)	n
	D>Accumulative:    	W  	n
	D>Duration:        	W 1 round / level 	n
	D>School of Magic: 	W Conjuration 	n
	D>Target(s):       	W All Enemies 	n
	D>Magic Resist:    	W No 	n
	D>Saving Throw:    	W No 	n
	D>Damage Type:     	W Force 	n
	D>Description:	n
	n
	nThis spell conjures forth large black tentacles from the ground which wrap
	nthemselves around any non-group members in the room, applying the entangle
	neffect with no saving throw allowed.  It also deals 1d6+4 force/crushing damage
	nper round.  Note that to receive experience from a creature dying from this
	neffect, you or another group member in your room must be fighting the creature
	nwhen it dies.
	n
	n
	n
	YSee also:	n SPELLS
	n
#0
CAUSTIC-BLOOD SPELL-CAUSTIC-BLOOD

	D>Usage:           	W cast 'caustic blood'	n
	D>Accumulative:    	W  	n
	D>Duration:        	W 1 round per level 	n
	D>School of Magic: 	W Transmutation 	n
	D>Target(s):       	W Self Only 	n
	D>Magic Resist:    	W No 	n
	D>Saving Throw:    	W Reflex (See Below) 	n
	D>Damage Type:     	W Acid 	n
	D>Description:	n
	n
	nYou imbue your blood with corrosive acid. Any time you take piercing or
	nslashing damage, a spray of acidic blood spurts from your body in the direction
	nof the opponent who inflicted the wound, dealing 1d6 points of acid damage per
	ncaster level (maximum 15d6, Reflex half). After it contacts a creature or
	nobject, your acidic blood continues to burn that creature for 1 round, dealing
	n1d6 points of acid damage per 2 caster levels (maximum 7d6). A second successful
	nReflex save negates this additional damage.
	n
	n
	n
	YSee also:	n SPELLS
	n
