#0
SPELLBATTLE

	c-----------------------------------------------------------------	n
	c>Usage:           	W spellbattle (lowest of: 12, caster level, BAB) 	n
	c>Prereqs:         	W Arcana Golem Only 	n
	c>Duration:        	W 6 Minutes 	n
	c>Target(s):       	W Self Only 	n
	c>Restrictions:    	W None 	n
	c>Cooldown:        	W 6 Minutes 	n
	c>Description:	n
	n
By channeling their inner magic, Arcana Golems can use it to provide a
huge surge to their physical attributes in the rare cases in which they
must resort to physical violence. While the eldritch energies cloud their
mind and finesse, the bonus to durability and power can provide that
edge when need.
	n
Spell Battle is a mode. When this mode is activated, you receive a penalty
to attack rolls equal to the argument and caster levels equal to half. In return,
you gain a bonus to AC and saving throws equal to the penalty taken,
a bonus to BAB equal to 2/3rds of this penalty (partially but not completely
negating the attack penalty), and a bonus to maximum hit points equal to 10
* penalty taken. Arcana Golems take an additional -2 penalty to Intelligence,
Wisdom, and Charisma while in Spell Battle.
	n
Spell battle without any arguments will cancel the mode, but an Arcana Golem
can only cancel Spell Battle after spending 10 minutes in it. The surge
of energy is not easily turned off.
	n
You cannot use Spell-Battle at the same time you use Power Attack, Combat
Expertise, or similar effects
	n
	YSee also:	n  SKILLS COMBAT-EXPERTISE POWER-ATTACK
	n
#0
SPELLBOOK

Wizards power does not come from raw talent, but
from intense studying of arcane texts.  A wizard's
spellbook is the collection of spells he/she has
gathered through his/her adventures.

See Also:  SCRIBE

#0
SPELLCRAFT

Usage:  Automatic

Spellcraft allows the individual to identify spells being
cast.  In addition, very high Spellcraft allows access
to Epic Spells.

See also:  EPIC-SPELLS
#0
SPELLLIST

Usage:  spelllist <class name> 
        spelllist <class name> <circle>
 
This command allows you to see all spells your class will get based
on the circle of spells.
 
To see what spells you currently have access to at your level, use
the SPELLS command.
 
See also: SKILLS SPELLS
#0
SPELLRECALL SPELL-RECALL

Usage: spellrecall

Spell Recall is a wizard perk that can be used once per real-world day. It
instantly completes one randomly selected spell currently being prepared. For
spontaneous caster levels, it instead immediately recovers one randomly selected
spell slot. Spell Recall is not consumed when there is nothing to recover.

See also: PREPARATION PERKS SPELLS
#0
EXTRACTS SPELLS

The world of Luminari is filled with magic.  Spells allow for spectacular
effects such as healing, summoning monsters, destructive magics, etc.
 
Usage:  spells <class name>
        spells <class name> <circle>
        extracts 
        extracts <circle>

 
This command will show you what spells/extracts you currently can cast/imbibe based on your
level and the class selected.
 
If you want to see a list of all the spells you will eventually get, just
use the SPELLLIST command.
 
You can also use the MASTERLIST command to view a complete list of all
spells (or skills) in the game.
 
	YSee Also:	n  SPELLLIST MASTERLIST MAGIC
#0
SPELLSTAFF

	D-----------------------------------------------------------------	n
	k	K	D>Usage:	n	n	n            cast 'spellstaff' <spellname	K	D>
	k	K	D>Accumulative:	n	n	n     No
	k	K	D>Duration:	n	n	n         Permanent until discharged
	k	K	D>School of Magic:	n	n	n  None
	k	K	D>Target(s):	n	n	n        Held staff
	k	K	D>Magic Resist:	n	n	n     N/A
