SPIRIT

Usage: summon spirit
Usage: banish spirit
Usage: ask spirit <subject>

The spirit guide is available to all players under level 7.  The 
guide can provide vital information for new players and make an
easy transition into LuminariMUD.  Here is a list of things that
you can ask your personal spirit guide:

	YAREAS	n - A list of newbie friendly areas to discover and explore.
	YCRAFTING	n - A quick crafting tutorial and a free piece of equipment.
	YEQ	n - Will provide you with a basic set of gear.
	YFEATS	n - A quick tutorial covering the feats system.
	YPRACTICE	n - A quick tutorial covering skills that can be practiced.
	YSPELLS	n - A quick tutorial based on your class.
	YTOUR	n - A detailed tour of Ashenport, the first main city.
#0
SPIRITUAL-WEAPON

	D>Usage:           	W cast 'spiritual weapon'	n
	D>Accumulative:    	W  	n
	D>Duration:        	W 1 round / level 	n
	D>School of Magic: 	W Evocation 	n
	D>Target(s):       	W Self Only 	n
	D>Magic Resist:    	W Yes 	n
	D>Saving Throw:    	W N/A 	n
	D>Damage Type:     	W Force 	n
	D>Description:	n
	n
	nThis spell conjures a spiritual weapon, whose type is based on the caster's
	nalignment. This weapon will attack the caster's foe every round. It will use the
	ncaster's base attack bonus (BAB) + their wisdom bonus against the enemy's armor
	nclass. If the caster has multiple attacks from their BAB, then the weapon will
	nattack multiple times, accordingly. Upon hit the weapon will deal the normal
	nweapon damage, plus the caster's divine spellcasting level / 3 (max of 5). The
	nweapon can score critical hits, though the threat range and critical multiplier
	nare unaffected by any feats or effects the caster has. Attacks can be negated
	nwith spell resistance, and the damage type done is force damage.
	n
	n
	n
	YSee also:	n SPELLS
	n
#0
SPLITTING

Usage: split <amount to split>

Split is used to divide money equally amongst players in your group who are in 
the same room as you.  If you are in a group with four other people, all of 
whom are in the same room with you, and you type SPLIT 100, you will give each 
of the other four group members twenty coins each.  (100 coins is split five 
ways; you keep your share and give everyone else their share).

See also: AUTOSPLIT, FOLLOW, GROUP
#0
SPOT

Perception is the ability used to counter HIDE.  If you are not actively in
SPOT-MODE you will have a very difficult time finding hidden players/
monsters.

Notice, while in SPOT-MODE you will suffer double the movement rate
penalties.

See the HIDE help file for info about hide versus spot calculations.

See Also:  HIDE
