#0
STAFF-EVENT STAFFEVENT STAFF_EVENT

Staff-ran events are world-wide quests that combine some aspects of automation along with staff participation.
To see details just type: staffevent with no argument.
Staff:
Staffevent with no argument to list the implemented staff events
'Staffevent start <index number>' to start the given event
'Staffevent end <index number>' to end the event (early)
'Staffevent info <index number>' to view details about the event
#0
STAGGERED


When one is afflicted by the staggered affect, they are only able to take one
standard or one move action each round, instead of normally having one of each.

#0
STALWART STALWART-DEFENDER STALWARTDEFENDER

This help file is unfinished.
#0
STANDARD-ACTION

A standard action allows you to do something, most commonly to make an attack 
or cast a spell.
 
Some examples of standard actions include:
 
- Attacking a mobile or player (using either the 	Yhit	n or 	Ykill	n commands)
- Reading a scroll (using the 	Yrecite	n command)
- Firing a ranged weapon (using the 	Yfire	n command)
- Laying on hands (using the paladin ability 	Ylayonhands	n)
- Identifying an object (using the 	Ylore	n command)
- Taunting an enemy (using the 	Ytaunt	n command)
 
A standard action will be used as a move action if a command requires a move 
action when only a standard action is available.
 
If you do not have a standard action during a combat round, you will not make 
any attacks.
 
	YSee Also:	n Combat, Move-action, Swift-action
#0
STAT

Usage: stat [player | object | mobile | file] <name>
Usage: stat [ room | feat | affect | zone ] <variable, see below>

Gives information about players, monsters, and objects in the game.  The type
argument is optional.

STAT PLAYER will search only for players; useful for statting people with
names such as Red or Cityguard.

STAT OBJECT will search only for objects.

STAT MOBILE will search only for monsters.

STAT FILE is used to stat players who are not logged in; the information
displayed comes from the players file.

STAT SELF will do the same thing as typing STAT <YOUR NAME>.

STAT AFF <monster or player> will display affections, cooldowns and resistances.

STAT ROOM <room number> will stat a given room, no argument is current room

STAT FEAT <target mobile/player> will list the target's feats

STAT AFFECT <target mob/player> will list the affections of the target

STAT ZONE <zone number> will stat a given zone, no argument is current zone

Examples:
  > stat fido
  > stat player Welcor 
  > stat mobile Fade 
  > stat file Rumble 
  > stat object thunderbolt
  > stat self

See also: VSTAT, TSTAT, DETACH


New commands: scriptvar, account

#0
STATCAP

Usage:  statcap
.
Stats have caps above their 'natural' value (via buffs, gear).
.
These caps are determined by your class primarily, but other factors such
as certain skills (rage) and items (twilight) that can
increase your cap further.
.
#0
ATTRIBUTES CHARISMA CONSTITUTION DEXTERITY INTELLIGENCE STATISTICS STATS STRENGTH WISDOM

	n
Statistics (Stats)- How your character measures up mentally and physically.
All stats can affect untold outcomes in scenarios, and all stats can give
bonuses to your abilities.
	n
A list is below:
	n
Wisdom       - Bonus to will saving throws, bonus spells for divine casters
Constitution - Hit point bonus and fortitude saving throw bonus.
Dexterity    - Skill with ranged weapons, armor-class bonus and reflex
               saving throw bonus.
Charisma     - Affects shop prices (both selling and buying).  Bonus spells
               for certain arcane classes.
Strength     - Determines accuracy and damage with melee weapons.  Affects how
               much weight you can carry.
Intelligence - Affects how many abilities you can train per level.  Grants
               bonus spells for certain arcane classes.
	n   
	YSee also:	n 	Rhitroll, damroll, armor-class, bonus-stat-cap, dexterity-bonus	n
	n
#0
STEAL STEALING

Usage: steal <item> [target]

Use steal to steal gold or items from people.  The chance of not getting
caught depends on how well you have trained sleight of hand, and if the person
is asleep.

Examples:

  > steal gold drunk
  > steal sword mercenary
    (If it is wielded, only possible if he is sleeping)

See also: FLAGS

