	c>Try Again:       	n N/A 	n
	c>Action Required: 	n hide, move; sneak, swift 	n
	c>Action Consumed: 	n hide, move; sneak, swift 	n
	n
	c>Skill Modifications:	n
	n
Stealthy Feat will give you +2 to your stealth checks
Halflings will get a +2 bonus to their stealth checks
Druid form of panther will get a +4 bonus to their stealth checks
Trackless step will give +4 bonus when in nature
	n
	c>Description:	n
	n
The stealth skill will determine your ability to hide (from sight) and to
sneak (from others detecting your movement).  A breakdown of how the current
system works follows:
	n
Sneaking and hiding maneuvers work independently of each other, unless you
make sure to attempt to sneak, THEN attempt to hide.  In that case you will
enter a special stealth mode where you attempt to mask your movement from
others, AND mask your visibility from others.  The formula for the challenge
of attempting stealth is as follows:
	n
Your stealth skill + diceroll d20 + size-difference [versus]
Observer perception skill + 10 (if observing)
	n
	YSee also:	n  SKILLS PERCEPTION OBSERVING SNEAK HIDE SPOT LISTEN
	n
