#0
SWIFT-ACTION

A swift action consumes a very small amount of time and represents an 
expenditure of effort and energy. You can perform only a single swift action 
per turn.  With the selection of certain feats you can perform certain actions
 using a swift action that before required a move or standard action. 
 
Examples of swift actions include:
 
- Casting 'magic missile'
- Dropping coins
- Placing an item in a container during combat (on a failed skill-check)
 
	YSee Also:	n Combat, Standard-action, Move-action
#0
SWIM

Swim

The swim ability will allow access for the player to areas
that normally require small boats to access.

If you fail your swim check, the movement attempt will consume
a move-action.

#0
SWITCH-OPPONENTS

Usage:  hit/kill <target>

Prereq:  None

You can change opponents anytime in combat, but there is a tumble check required
to avoid being hit by your opponents as you make the switch in battle.

See also:  TUMBLE
