#0
TAILORING

   Tailoring is a crafting skill used to create clothing and other wearables\nmade from cloth.\n

#0
TAILSWEEP

Usage:  tailsweep

Some creatures are so large and have such powerful tails, that they are
able to swing their tails with enough force to attempt to knock down
everyone they are fighting.

See also:  INNATE
#0
TAME

Usage:  tame <intended mount>

Tame is a form of making a non-CHARMEE mount calm so you can ride the mount easier.  It will
reduce the chance the mount will BUCK or wander away.

See also:  MOUNT DISMOUNT CHARMEE BUCK
#0
TANK

   This individual is the leader of the group and takes the brunt of all 
attacks. 

See also: GROUP
#0
TANKING

Tanking is a term given to the player or mobile who
is the primary target of an opponents melee attacks.

#0
TAUNT

Usage:  taunt <target>

Prereq:  None

Taunt is an ability that drastically reduces AC and reduces
spell casting success for a very short time.  The skill itself
has about a 7 second cooldown.

The diplomacy skill is compared to the victim's concentration skill
to determine success.

See also:  CONCENTRATION
#0
TCOPY TRIGGER-COPY

This command will copy a trigger that already exists and duplicate it under a new vnum.
This command is not used often, as usually you can assign triggers to multiple sources if
they are the same thing.  However this command does have its uses such as when making
a trigger that will result in a same or similar function as the original but you're just
changing text or variables.

Usage: tcopy <vnum> <vnum>
#0
TEAMWORK-FEATS


 Teamwork feats are feats that only benefit you if another member of your
party also has the same teamwork feat.  Generally speaking they are more
powerful than regular feats, given the requirement that another party
member must have the same teamwork feat in order for you to benefit from it.

Inquisitors eventually get the solo tactics class ability, which allows them
to benefit from teamwork feats, even if other party members don't have it.

There is also a 'teamwork' class ability for Inquisitors, not to be
confused with teamwork feats itself.  The teamwork class ability
actually grants the Inquisitor 1 teamwork feat of their choice for
each rank.

