#0
TINKER TINKERING


Usage: tinker (weapon or armor chest piece name)

Rock gnomes have the ability to tinker with existing weapons and armor
to improve their effectiveness temporarily.  They can specify any weapon
in their inventory, or any body/chest piece of armor in their inventory.

Once tinkered, weapons get a +1 to attack rolls, and a +1 to damage rolls
if wielded one handed, or +2 if it's a two handed melee weapon. Armor chest
pieces will bestow an additional +1 Armor bonus to AC.

These effects disappear if the character quits from the game, or if there's
a copyover or any o game downtime reason.

#0
TITLES

Usage: title <new title>

Sets the title people see on the WHO list and when you're in the room with
them.  You can't use parentheses (the ( and ) characters) because those
are reserved for flags.

Do not create offensive titles or your title will be set for you.

See also: FLAGS, WHO, NOTITLE
#0
TNL

   An acronym for to next level. The amount of experience required before you 
can attain the next level.

#0
TODO TODO-LIST

	n
TODO "TODO LIST"
	n
The todo command allows you to keep a todo list saved to your
character.  It doesn't do anything but keep track of what you tell it
to.
	n
	cUsage:	n todo [thing to do | # to delete] 
	n
'Todo' with no arguments will display your current todo list.
	n
	wExamples:	n
  todo Build mines.  - adds "Build mines." to your todo list
  todo 1             - Deletes todo #1
  show todo Fizban   - Lists what is on Fizban's TODO list.
	n
#0
TOGGLES

Usage: toggle
       toggle <option> <argument>

*NOTE* It's easier to use prefedit

TOGGLE shows you the current values of various toggles available on the MUD.
This command can also be used to change these values, if used with the correct
argument. When a toggle is set, it will be saved in that state until the next
time you change it. Level IMP toggle includes:

 SlowNameserver: OFF                            Trackthru Doors: ON 
      Buildwalk: OFF              NoWiz: OFF             ClsOLC: OFF
       NoHassle: ON           Holylight: ON           ShowVnums: ON 
         Syslog: normal
Hit Pnt Display: OFF              Brief: OFF         Summonable: OFF
   Move Display: OFF            Compact: ON               Quest: OFF
   Mana Display: OFF             NoTell: OFF           NoRepeat: OFF
      AutoExits: OFF            NoShout: OFF              Wimpy: OFF
       NoGossip: OFF          NoAuction: OFF            NoGrats: OFF
       AutoLoot: ON            AutoGold: ON           AutoSplit: ON 
        AutoSac: ON          AutoAssist: ON             AutoMap: ON
     Pagelength: 32         Screenwidth: 80                 AFK: OFF
        Autokey: OFF           Autodoor: OFF              Color: on     

See also: DISPLAY, NOSHOUT, NOSUMM, NOTELL, QUEST, REPEAT, WIMP, PREFEDIT
#0
TOTAL-DEFENSE TOTALDEFENSE

Usage:  totaldefense

When in blocking mode, you forfeit all your attacks in an attempt
to deflect your opponent(s) attacks.  The challenge of the totaldefense is
your opponents attack roll vs. your totaldefense skill.

In the case that you beat your opponents challenge by 10 or more, you
will get a counter-attack "riposte" in addition to totaldefenseing their
attack.

You can only totaldefense the number of incoming attacks equal to your
current number of attacks.

See also:  ATTACK

