#0
TRAP-OBJECTS TRAPS

	n
	YTrap Objects for OLC	n
	n
Besides using Scripts to create various forms of traps to throw up
against a player, we also have a trap system in place that will
utilize the 'perception' and 'disable device' skills/abilities that
players can train.
	n
To create a trap, create a new item with the trap item-type set, then
set a L-Desc starting with a period (.) so the object will be invisible
to players.  You will then want to zedit the room you want the trap to
be set, and load the trap object to that room.
	n
	YTrap Types	n
	n
The types will respond when you place the trap object in the room:
Enter Room - The trap will fire when you enter the room
Open Door - Opening a door with the assigned direction on the trap will
            cause the trap to fire
Unlock Door - Unlocking a door with the assigned direction on the trap
              will cause the trap to fire
Open Container - Opening a container with the assigned vnum on the trap
                 will cause it to fire
Unlock Container - Unlocking a container with the assigned vnum will
                   cause the trap to fire
	n
	YTrap Effects	n
	n
You can either select a spellnum (use 	Rmasterlist spells	n to see the
spellnum for various spells) or select a special effect from the list:
  "Wall of Flames" 20d20 fire damage
  "Lightning Strike"20d30 electric damage
  "Impaling Spike" 15d20 piercing damage, paralysis 5 rounds
  "Dark Glyph" 300 + 15d20 mental damage, feeblemind (-10 int) 25 rounds
  "Spike Pit" 2d10 piercing damage
  "Harmful Dart" 10 + 6d6 piercing damage
  "Poison Gas" 15 + 2d15 poison damage, poison 25 rounds
  "Dispel Magic" level 34 dispel magic
  "Dark Warrior Ambush" 1-3 (depending on level) dark warriors hunts ch
  "Boulder Drop" 1/5th of current hps force damage
  "Wall Smash" 1/5th of current hps force damage
  "Spider Horde" 1/6th of current hps force damage
  "Harmful Gas" 1/4th of current hps poison damage
  "Freezing Conditions" 10d20 cold damage
  "Skeletal Hands" 50% chance for death, otherwise 10d40 cold damage
  "Spider Webs" 20 rounds webbed (grapple) effect and 1-3 spiders hunt ch
	n
	YTrap DC	n
	n
Recommended DC's for traps:
DC = 20 + level-of-trap for a normal trap
DC = 30 + level-of-trap for a hard trap
DC = 40 + level-of-trap for an epic trap
	n
	YDealing With Traps	n
	n
Finding traps currently uses the command 	Rdetecttrap	n and disarming a
trap currently uses the command 	Rdisabletrap	n.  Detecting a trap will
use a perception check versus the trap DC, and disarming the trap will
use a disable-device check versus the trap DC.
	n
	YSee Also:	n DISABLETRAP DETECTTRAP PERCEPTION DISABLE-DEVICE
	n
