#0
UNASSIGNPILOT

Usage: unassignpilot

Removes the currently assigned NPC pilot from the vessel. This will
also stop the autopilot if it is currently running.

Requirements:
- You must be the captain of the vessel
- The vessel must have a pilot currently assigned

After removing the pilot:
- Autopilot will be disengaged if it was active
- Manual autopilot control will be required to navigate
- The NPC will remain in the helm room but no longer controls the ship

To assign a new pilot, use the ASSIGNPILOT command.

See also: ASSIGNPILOT, AUTOPILOT, SETROUTE
#0
UNBIND

This command will unbind an object from a players ID.

Usage: unbind <object>

SEE ALSO: obind
#0
BLOODLINE-UNDEAD SORCERER-BLOODLINE-UNDEAD UNDEAD-BLOODLINE


The taint of the grave runs through your family. Perhaps one of
your ancestors became a powerful lich or vampire, or maybe you were born dead
before suddenly returning to life. Either way, the forces of death move through
you and touch your every action. The undead sorcerer bloodline allows you to
cause fear in opponents, gain resistance to cold and innate damage reduction,
cause the dead to reach forth from the earth to ravage your foes, become
incorporeal and eventually become one of the undead yourself. 
 
NEW CLASS SKILL: Intimidate

BONUS SPELLS: chill touch (3rd), false life (5th), vampiric touch (7th), animate dead (9th),
waves of fatigue (11th), undeath to death (13th), finger of death (15th), horrid wilting (17th),
energy drain (19th)
 
CLASS FEATS: combat casting, diehard, endurance, iron will, spell focus, skill focus, still spell,
toughness
 
The undead bloodline also gives the following bonus abilities:
Undead are succeptible to your mind-affecting spells at level 1. (HELP UNDEAD ARCANA)
Can cause shaken affect with a touch at level 1. (HELP GRAVE TOUCH)
Gain cold and nonlethal resistance, and damage reduction at level 3. (HELP DEATH'S TOUCH)
Can cause skeletal arms to grasp at your foes at level 9. (HELP GRASP OF THE DEAD)
Can become incorporeal at level 15. (HELP INCORPOREAL FORM)
Become immune to cold and nonlethal damage, sleep and paralysis affects as well, more
damage reduction, will not aggro undead NPCs, and gain a +4 to saving throws against
spells and abilities by undead foes. (HELP ONE OF US)
 
See Also: SORCERER
#0
UNDEAD-RACE

There are some playable undead races in the game.  Being undead, wether as a playable race or NPC has
very distinct advantages and disadvantages.  A list of them follows, but is not limited to:
- NPC mobs that are cleric or paladin class will try to turn undead (including players)
- Any undead will be healed by a lich's touch attack
- All undead are vulnerable to sunlight bombs (from Alchemists)
- All undead are vulnerable to the 'veil of positive energy' spell
- NPC undead that die will not leave a corpse
- All undead are vulnerable to the 'life shield' spell
- All undead are invulnerable to vampiric curse attacks
- All undead are invulnerable to 'vampiric touch' spells/spell-like affects
- Undead can't drown
- NPC Undead will not attack those with the 'One of Us' feat
- All undead are vulnerable to the 'searing light' spell
- All undead are vulnerable to the 'undeath to death' spell
- All undead are vulnerable to the 'halt undead' spell
- All undead can benefit from the 'strengthen bone' spell
- All undead are immune to negative energy channel
- All undead are vulnerable to positive energy channel
- All undead are immune to critical attacks
- All undead are immune to mind-affecting spells
- All undead are immune to disease
- All undead are immune to poison
See also: race info vampire, race info lich
