#0
VALUE

Usage: value <item>

Before selling an item to a shop, you can ask the shopkeeper how much
he or she is willing to pay for it.
 
Example:
 
  > value bread
 
See also: BUY, LIST, SELL, SHOPS
#0
SETCLOAK VAMPIRE-CLOAK


Usage: setcloak (apply type)
       setcloak description (new description)

A vampire's cloak is a specially enchanted item that both protects the
vampire from the damage of the sun as well as offer them a bonus
that the vampire can choose themselves.

To see what bonuses are available, while wearing the cloak, simply
type in: 	Ysetcloak	n by itself, and that will display a list.

To assign a certain bonus to the cloak, type in: 	Ysetcloak (bonus type)	n.
This bonus can only be set once every ten minutes or so.

A vampire can also restring his cloak at any time by typing in:
	Ysetcloak description (new description)	n.
Note that the cloak must be worn to restring it.

If a vampire loses their cloak, currently they need to ask a staff
member to replace it.

As of this writing, the vampire cloak vnum is 34700.

#0
VAMPIRE-DOMINATE

Usage: dominate (target)

A vampire can attempt to dominate any sentient being at will using the
dominate command.  If successful the target will become charmed
and under the vampire's control.

All normal conditions and resistances for charm are applicable.

See Also: VAMPIRIC-DOMINATE

#0
VAMPIRE-GASEOUS-FORM

Usage: gaseousform

A vampire can assume a gaseous state at-will.  While in this state he
receives 1/2 damage from physical attacks, unless the attacker
is incorporeal themselves, or wielding a ghost-touch weapon.

The reverse is true as well.  The vampire deals 1/2 damage on
physical attacks unless their target is also incorporeal or the
vampire is using a ghost touch weapon.

See Also: SPELL-GASEOUS-FORM

#0
VAMPIRE-FORM VAMPIREFORM

Usage: vampireform (wolf|bat)

A vampire can shape change into a wolf or bat at-will using the vampireform command.

To see info on the vampire race, type 	Yrace info vampire	n.
