	nvitriolic blast. A vitriolic blast deals acid damage, and is formed from
	nconjured acid, making it different from all other eldritch essences because it
	nignores spell resistance. Creatures struck by a vitriolic blast automatically
	ntake an extra 2d6 points of acid damage on following rounds. This acid damage
	npersists for 1 round per five class levels you have. For example, a 15th-level
	nwarlock deals 2d6 points of acid damage per round for 3 rounds after the initial
	nvitriolic blast attack.
