#0
APPLY-OIL APPLYOIL SET-BANE-WEAPON SETBANEWEAPON WEAPON-OILS WEAPONOILS


Usage: applyoil (weapon in inventory) (oil object)
       setbaneweapon (racial type) (optional subrace type)

Weapon oils are usually found as a reward for trading in hunt trophies at a huntsmaster.
When applied to a weapon, it will add the special ability associated with the weapon
oil to the weapon specified.  Note that in most cases, weapon oils can't be added to
a weapon that already has a special ability.

Some weapon special abilities can be enhanced.  See the following table for more info:
Flaming Weapons   : Can be upgraded to flaming burst with flaming weapon oil
Corrosive Weapons : Can be upgraded to corrosive burst with corrosive weapon oil
Frost Weapons     : Can be upgraded to icy burst with frost weapon oil
Shock Weapons     : Can be upgraded to shocking burst with shock weapon oil

Also, some weapon oils can only be added to certain weapon types, like ranged weapons
only, or light weapons only.

See Also: HUNTS, WEAPON-ABILITIES

#0
WEAPON-PROF

Simple Weapon Proficiency
Elf Weapon Proficiency
Druid Weapon Proficiency
Martial Weapon Proficiency
Exotic Weapon Proficiency

Every class starts with at least "simple" weapon proficiencies.  Advancement with
weapon proficiencies occur as follows:

Elven and Druid Weapon Proficiency require Simple Weapon Proficiency
Martial Weapon Proficiency requires either Elven or Druid Weapon Proficiency
Exotic Weapon Proficiency requires Martial Weapon Proficiency

See also:  ARMOR-PROF
