#0
WILDERNESS

Welcome to the jungle!  Our wilderness system is a map, co-ordinate based
system used to navigate the 'surface' of our Realm.  Instead of 'road zones'
that are typical of old-skool MUDs, we designed a massive expansive world-map.

The wilderness system is currently under construction, so pardon our dust.
Besides serving as a tool to connect our zones, we have in development, unique
system such as random encounters, specialized traveling system and a special
region system.

The region system will help us draw areas onto the wilderness that will directly
affect the experience.  Example is if we drew a region around the city of
Ashenport, whenever you approached close to that region, details about that
region would influence the wilderness-room descriptions.

Bare with us, we are excited to release more and more exciting and unique
features built on this system!

*You can type MAP in wilderness to get a larger view of where you are at.
*We are marking most connected zones to the wilderness with a 	RX	n, but
     some zones are hidden with natural things such as broken roads leading
      into the zone
*We have placed portals next to major towns that connect them, undecided
    if they will remain as we develop travel methods

#0
WILDSHAPE WILDSHAPE-RETURN

Druids have the ability to shapechange into a selection of animals
and other creatures based on level and feats.  Depending on the form
taken you can acquire stat bonuses and other special abilities.  The
druid with proper knowledge of their abilities will be able to tackle
nearly any situation using their shape-shifting abilities.

To leave your wild shaped form and return to your original body,
type: wildshape return

See also: 	Rshapechange	n

#0
DRAGON-FORM WILDSHAPE-DRAGON-FORMS WILDSHAPE-DRAGONS

Usage: wildshape (red dragon|blue dragon|green dragon|black dragon|white dragon)
-----: dragonfear
-----: breathe
-----: dragonmagic (target) (detect-magic|continual-flame|dispel-magic|invisibility)
-----: dragonmagic (target) (see-invisibility|shield|true-strike|endure-elements}
-----: dragonmagic (target) (magic missile|haste) 	Rred dragons only	n
-----: dragonmagic (target) (mage-armor|lightning bolt) 	Cblue dragons only	n
-----: dragonmagic (target) (mage-armor|mirror-image) 	Ggreen dragons only	n
-----: dragonmagic (target) (stinking-cloud|slow) 	Dblack dragons only	n
-----: dragonmagic (target) (chill-touch|ice-storm) 	Wwhite dragons only	n

The Chromatic Dragon types are a wildshape option for members of the shifter prestige class.
They have 5 damage reduction and 25 spell resistance.  They are able to breathe an
area of effect attack once every 2 combat rounds, dealing elemental damage coinciding
with their dragon type: red=fire, blue=lightning, green=poison, black=acid, white=cold.
They also have high resistance against elemental damage coinciding with their dragon type.
Red and white dragons also have vulnerability to cold and fire damage respectively.

Dragons can cause fear to all enemies in the room as a swift action by typing dragonfear.

Dragons are also able to cast certain magic spells, with some variation between dragon types.

