#31
HLQEDIT-DIALOGUE

After completing the quest-in (quest entries) and the quest-out
(quest reward) aspect of a quest, the final step is to fill out
the dialogue entry.  You will be sent to the text-editor to
write/edit the output you want.  You can use $N to refer to the
quest-mobile's name if you need.  Example:

If the quest mobile is a 'beastly fido':
$N scarfs down the meat!
$N rubs against you thankfully!

This would result in:
The beastly fido scarfs down the meat!
The beastly fido rubs against you thankfully!

