#31
MOB-LIT

A mobile with a 'lit' flag will make sure the mobile is lit
regardless of its sight restrictions or the light-levels of
the room.

See Also:  MOB-FLAGS

#31
MOB-PATHS

Mob-paths (option V in medit) is a tool to help set up patrolling
mobiles.  It is very simple to use, but its best to follow this
procedure for the smoothest paths:

1)  Decide on a path of rooms you want your mobile to patrol
before modifying the path.  You will want to collect a list of
room vnums to determine this path (NOT directional choices).

2)  The first option you will be prompted to choose upon creating
a path is the 'delay.'  The delay will determine how many 'mobile
ticks' before the mobile will follow the next direction in the path.
To get a feel for it, you can play with this value, we suggest a value
of 3 for a higher-speed patrol, and a value of 6 for a more casual
patrol.

3)  You will then be prompted to start entering room-vnum values for
the path you want your mobile to try and follow.  You will be entering
values one-per-line and you can terminate the sequence with a line of
just the value '0' on it.

4)  The final and probably most important step is to have any staff
member with the switch command, to use the 'switch' command into your
mobile to observe its path, a fairly thorough debugging set of info
will be broadcasted to the mobile while on a path.

If you have any questions, feel free to ask the head-builder or any of
the forgers.

See Also:  MEDIT

